(function(){
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const E=(w,origin)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:'Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/'+w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')});
const Q=(id,senseId,errorType,prompt,answer,d1,d2,explain)=>({id,senseId,type:'辨義與用法',errorType,prompt,options:[answer,d1,d2],answer,explain});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistakes,quiz)=>D(w,{etymology:E(w,origin),contexts,mistakes,quiz});
P('tragic','From Latin tragicus and Greek tragikos, “of or relating to tragedy.”',[C('tragic.s1','事故与悲痛','The family described the preventable fire as a tragic loss that changed their lives.','這家人把本可避免的火災稱為一場改變人生的悲劇性損失。','tragic + event, loss, or consequence','Adjective: causing great sadness, especially through death or suffering.','The fire caused deep grief and lasting harm.'),C('tragic.s2','戏剧文学','The play gives its tragic hero a final chance to admit his mistake.','這齣戲讓悲劇英雄有最後一次承認錯誤的機會。','tragic + hero, play, or ending','Adjective: relating to drama with a sad ending.','The character and play belong to the tragic dramatic form.')],[M('The cheerful picnic with no loss or suffering was a tragic disaster.','The cheerful picnic ended happily and caused no tragic loss.','Tragic describes great sadness or a drama with a sad ending, not a happy event.')],[Q('tragic.q1','tragic.s1','meaning','Why was the fire called a tragic loss?','It caused profound sadness and suffering.','It was a pleasant surprise with no consequences.','It was a comedy performed on stage.','The first sense describes an event that causes great sadness.'),Q('tragic.q2','tragic.s2','context','What is a tragic hero in a play?','A central character in a drama with a sad outcome.','A comic side character who never faces difficulty.','A stage worker who sells tickets.','Tragic can describe plays and heroes associated with sad endings.'),Q('tragic.q3','tragic.s1','distinction','Which event is most naturally called tragic?','A preventable accident that kills several people.','A routine meeting that ends five minutes early.','A lively festival with music and dancing.','Death and profound grief fit the event-related sense.'),Q('tragic.q4','tragic.s2','grammar','Which phrase uses tragic in its dramatic sense?','a tragic drama about a doomed king','a tragic teaspoon in the kitchen','a tragic increase that caused no sadness','The drama has the sad ending associated with tragedy.')]);
P('trail','Recorded in Middle English for dragging or following; its deeper origin is uncertain.',[C('trail.s1','户外路线','The marked trail climbs through pine woods before reaching the lake.','有標記的小徑穿過松林，最後通往湖邊。','a trail through / to + place','Noun: a path through countryside or a forest.','The marked route leads through the woods.'),C('trail.s2','留下的痕迹','Wet boots left a trail of muddy prints across the hall.','濕靴子在走廊上留下一串泥腳印。','a trail of + marks or evidence','Noun: a line of marks or signs left behind.','The prints form a visible line showing where someone walked.'),C('trail.s4','比赛比分','At halftime, the visitors trailed by one goal.','半場時，客隊落後一球。','trail by + amount','Verb: be behind an opponent in a contest.','The visitors have a lower score.')],[M('At halftime the visitors trailed by one goal, so they were ahead on the scoreboard.','At halftime the visitors trailed by one goal, so they were behind on the scoreboard.','To trail by a goal is to have a lower score, not to lead.')],[Q('trail.q1','trail.s1','meaning','What does a marked forest trail provide?','A path to follow through the countryside.','A list of railway carriages.','A score showing a team is ahead.','Trail in this sense is a path through a natural area.'),Q('trail.q2','trail.s2','context','What can a trail of wet footprints show?','The route someone took across the floor.','That the floor has no marks at all.','That a team won by two points.','A trail can be a line of marks left behind.'),Q('trail.q3','trail.s4','distinction','If a team trails by three points, what is true?','It is three points behind its opponent.','It is three points ahead.','The match has not started.','The competition sense means being behind in score.'),Q('trail.q4','trail.s1','word-choice','Which phrase refers to a countryside path?','a trail beside the river','a trainload beside the river','a trait beside the river','A trail is the route hikers can follow.')]);
P('trailer','Formed from trail + -er; the vehicle sense names something drawn behind another vehicle.',[C('trailer.s1','运输','The boat was secured to a trailer before the family drove to the lake.','一家人開車去湖邊前，先把船固定在拖車上。','tow / load something onto a trailer','Noun: a vehicle or container pulled behind a car or lorry.','The car pulls the container carrying the boat.'),C('trailer.s2','影视宣传','The studio released a short trailer before the film opened.','電影上映前，片商先發布了一段短預告片。','release / watch a film trailer','Noun: a short film advertising an upcoming programme or movie.','The preview shows scenes to attract future viewers.')],[M('The studio called its full three-hour feature a trailer released to advertise itself.','The studio released a short trailer to advertise its upcoming three-hour feature.','A trailer is a short preview, not the full film.')],[Q('trailer.q1','trailer.s1','meaning','What does a road trailer do?','It is pulled behind a vehicle to carry a load.','It advertises a film with a short preview.','It powers the car from the front wheels.','The first sense is a container or vehicle towed behind another vehicle.'),Q('trailer.q2','trailer.s2','context','Why might viewers watch a film trailer?','To see a brief preview before deciding about the film.','To carry a boat on a highway.','To read the film’s complete transcript.','A film trailer advertises an upcoming movie with selected scenes.'),Q('trailer.q3','trailer.s1','distinction','Which object is a trailer in the vehicle sense?','A small box on wheels hitched behind a car.','A short preview shown before a cinema release.','A person learning to repair engines.','The hitched box is pulled behind the car.'),Q('trailer.q4','trailer.s2','word-choice','Which sentence uses trailer for an advertisement?','The trailer revealed the film’s dramatic opening scene.','The trailer carried camping gear behind the car.','The trailer repaired the railway signal.','The sentence describes a preview of a film.')]);
P('train','From Old French trainer, ultimately Latin trahere “to draw”; the rail sense developed for a connected line of carriages.',[C('train.s1','铁路交通','We took the last train home after the concert ended.','音樂會結束後，我們搭了末班火車回家。','catch / take a train','Noun: a series of railway carriages pulled by an engine.','The passengers travel in rail carriages connected to an engine.'),C('train.s3','教学与准备','The clinic will train new nurses to use the monitoring equipment.','診所將訓練新護士使用監測設備。','train someone to do something','Verb: teach a person or animal a skill, or prepare for an activity.','The nurses are being taught practical skills.'),C('train.s4','瞄准','The photographer trained her lens on the stage.','攝影師把鏡頭對準舞台。','train a camera / gun on + target','Verb: point a camera or weapon deliberately at something.','The lens is directed toward a specific target.')],[M('The clinic trained new nurses, meaning it placed them on a railway carriage.','The clinic trained new nurses by teaching them clinical skills.','Train as a verb can mean teach or prepare, not put someone on a train.')],[Q('train.q1','train.s1','meaning','What is a passenger train?','Connected railway carriages pulled by an engine.','A person learning a new job.','A lens deliberately pointed at a stage.','The transport noun names the connected rail carriages and engine.'),Q('train.q2','train.s3','context','If a clinic trains nurses, what does it do?','It teaches them skills needed for their work.','It sends them on a railway without lessons.','It points a camera at them.','The verb sense means teach or prepare someone.'),Q('train.q3','train.s4','distinction','What happened when the photographer trained her lens on the actor?','She pointed the lens toward the actor.','She taught the actor how to drive a train.','She attached the lens to a railway carriage.','Train on means aim or direct toward a target.'),Q('train.q4','train.s1','word-choice','Which phrase clearly uses train as transport?','They missed the train to the coast.','They train the dog to sit.','She trained a camera on the moon.','The coast-bound train is the railway vehicle.')]);
P('trainee','Formed from train + -ee, naming the person receiving instruction or preparation.',[C('trainee.s1','职场培训','Each trainee shadows an experienced electrician before working alone.','每位受訓者在獨立工作前，都會跟隨一名資深電工學習。','a trainee in / for + role','Noun: a person learning the skills needed for a job.','The trainee is learning the occupation under supervision.')],[M('The company called the senior instructor a trainee, although she was teaching everyone else.','The company called the new learner a trainee while the senior instructor taught her.','A trainee receives training; the instructor provides it.')],[Q('trainee.q1','trainee.s1','meaning','Who is a trainee electrician?','A person learning the work of an electrician.','A person who only teaches experienced electricians.','A vehicle pulled behind a car.','A trainee is learning job skills, often at the start of a role.'),Q('trainee.q2','trainee.s1','context','Why does a trainee shadow an experienced worker?','To learn practical skills before working independently.','To prove that training has already ended.','To pull a trainload of equipment.','Shadowing provides supervised job learning.'),Q('trainee.q3','trainee.s1','distinction','Which person is the trainee?','The new nurse being taught how to use the equipment.','The supervisor teaching the whole team.','The patient receiving a blood transfusion.','The learner, rather than the instructor, is the trainee.'),Q('trainee.q4','trainee.s1','grammar','Choose the natural phrase.','a trainee for the laboratory role','a trainee the instructor by the classroom','a trainee of train carriages','Trainee commonly identifies the learner in a role or programme.')]);
P('trainer','From train + -er; British English also uses trainer for a soft sports shoe.',[C('trainer.s1','体育教学','The trainer adjusted the runner’s schedule after the injury.','跑者受傷後，教練調整了他的訓練安排。','a trainer prepares / coaches someone','Noun: a person who teaches a skill or prepares someone for sport.','The person guides the runner’s practice.'),C('trainer.s2','鞋类','She packed a pair of trainers for the gym.','她帶了一雙運動鞋去健身房。','a pair of trainers (British)','Noun: a soft shoe for sport or casual wear, especially in British English.','The plural refers to athletic footwear.')],[M('The athlete tied her trainers before asking the coach to design a workout.','The athlete tied her trainers before asking the trainer to design a workout.','In British English trainers are shoes, while a trainer can also be the coach.')],[Q('trainer.q1','trainer.s1','meaning','What does a sports trainer do?','Teaches or prepares an athlete to improve.','Provides shoes by pulling them behind a car.','Records a student’s course grades.','The person sense refers to a coach or instructor.'),Q('trainer.q2','trainer.s2','context','In British English, what might someone pack for the gym?','A pair of trainers, meaning sports shoes.','A trainload of coaches.','A film preview.','Trainers is a common British term for sports shoes.'),Q('trainer.q3','trainer.s1','distinction','Which use means a person rather than footwear?','The trainer planned hill workouts for the runner.','He cleaned his trainers after practice.','She bought new trainers for the gym.','Planning workouts is the coach’s role.'),Q('trainer.q4','trainer.s2','word-choice','Which sentence uses trainer for a shoe?','His muddy trainers were left by the door.','The trainer taught the team to serve.','A trainee joined the workshop.','Muddy trainers by a door are sports shoes.')]);
P('training','From train + -ing; it can name instruction for a task or physical preparation.',[C('training.s1','职业技能','The new laboratory staff completed safety training before handling chemicals.','新實驗室員工在接觸化學品前完成了安全訓練。','training in / for + skill or job','Noun: instruction that teaches practical skills for a job or task.','The staff learned procedures they need for their work.'),C('training.s2','体育锻炼','Her daily training included hill runs and recovery sessions.','她每天的訓練包括山地跑和恢復練習。','physical training / training for an event','Noun: exercise to stay fit or prepare for a competition.','The runs are part of physical preparation.')],[M('The staff skipped safety training, so they learned nothing about handling chemicals.','The staff completed safety training to learn how to handle chemicals.','Training is the instruction or exercise itself, not the absence of learning.')],[Q('training.q1','training.s1','meaning','What is workplace safety training?','Instruction in procedures needed to work safely.','A person who learns the procedures.','A film preview about the laboratory.','Training can be organized instruction for a job or task.'),Q('training.q2','training.s2','context','Why might an athlete do daily training?','To build fitness and prepare for an event.','To obtain a transcript of school grades.','To move a vehicle from one place to another.','The physical sense is exercise for fitness or competition.'),Q('training.q3','training.s1','distinction','Which example is job training?','A new cashier practices using the payment system with a supervisor.','A runner completes a hill workout.','A train carries passengers across the country.','Practicing a work system with a supervisor is instruction for a job.'),Q('training.q4','training.s2','word-choice','Which phrase clearly means physical preparation?','three weeks of marathon training','a trainee in accounting','a training manual for cashiers','Marathon training refers to the exercise needed for the race.')]);
P('trainload','A compound of train + load, meaning the amount or contents carried by one train.',[C('trainload.s1','铁路货运','A trainload of wheat arrived at the port before the storm.','一整列火車的小麥在暴風雨前抵達港口。','a trainload of + cargo or people','Noun: as much as one train can carry, or what one train carries.','The shipment fills the carrying capacity of a train.')],[M('One small sack of wheat was described as a trainload, though the train carried thousands of sacks.','Thousands of sacks filled a trainload of wheat.','Trainload refers to a train’s load or contents, not one small item.')],[Q('trainload.q1','trainload.s1','meaning','What does a trainload of wheat mean?','The quantity of wheat carried by one train.','A single passenger ticket.','A person learning to operate a train.','Trainload names what one train can carry or does carry.'),Q('trainload.q2','trainload.s1','context','A trainload of passengers arrived together. What does the phrase emphasize?','The large group carried on one train.','That every passenger drove a separate car.','That the train had no passengers.','The compound focuses on the train’s cargo or passenger capacity.'),Q('trainload.q3','trainload.s1','distinction','Which item could be described as a trainload?','All the timber carried by one freight train.','A timetable for one station.','One coach teaching a class.','A freight train’s full cargo is a trainload.'),Q('trainload.q4','trainload.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural sentence.','A trainload of coal left the mine at dawn.','A trainload of coal taught the miners to read.','A trainload of coal means one coal particle.','A trainload can be a full quantity of cargo transported by one train.')]);
P('trait','From French trait “stroke, feature,” from Latin tractus, a drawing or line.',[C('trait.s1','人格特征','Patience is a useful trait for anyone working with young children.','對於與幼兒共事的人來說，耐心是一種有用的性格特徵。','a trait of / in someone','Noun: a particular quality in a person’s character.','Patience describes a characteristic of the worker.'),C('trait.s2','遗传与特征','Researchers compared the inherited trait across several plant varieties.','研究人員比較了幾種植物品系中的遺傳性狀。','an inherited / physical trait','Noun: a distinguishing quality of a living thing or object.','The quality varies among the plant varieties.')],[M('The study called a shared leaf shape a personality trait in a group of plants.','The study called a shared leaf shape a distinguishing trait of the plant group.','Trait can describe a distinguishing quality of an organism, but personality is specific to people.')],[Q('trait.q1','trait.s1','meaning','Patience is what kind of trait in a caregiver?','A characteristic of the caregiver’s personality.','A railway carriage pulled by an engine.','A printed copy of a speech.','The character sense is a quality of a person.'),Q('trait.q2','trait.s2','context','What is an inherited trait in a plant study?','A distinguishing quality passed from one generation to another.','A score showing the plant is losing.','A path through a forest.','The biological sense is a distinguishing quality of a living thing.'),Q('trait.q3','trait.s1','distinction','Which is a personality trait?','Being patient when a task takes time.','Having a transparent glass container.','Carrying grain by rail.','Patience is a quality of someone’s character.'),Q('trait.q4','trait.s2','word-choice','Which phrase fits a study of genetics?','an inherited trait such as seed colour','a trainload of seed colour','a film trailer of seed colour','Seed colour can be a distinguishing inherited characteristic.')]);
P('traitor','From Old French traitor and Latin traditor, “one who hands over or betrays.”',[C('traitor.s1','忠诚与背叛','The officer was branded a traitor after secretly giving the defence plans to the enemy.','那名軍官暗中把防禦計畫交給敵人後，被斥為叛徒。','a traitor to + group or cause','Noun: a person who betrays a friend, organization, or country.','He deliberately betrayed the side to which he owed loyalty.')],[M('She protected the confidential plans and served her country loyally, so everyone called her a traitor.','She secretly gave the confidential plans to the enemy, so people called her a traitor.','A traitor betrays a group or country; loyal protection is the opposite.')],[Q('traitor.q1','traitor.s1','meaning','Why is the officer called a traitor?','He secretly gave his side’s plans to its enemy.','He protected the plans and remained loyal.','He taught new officers a skill.','A traitor is disloyal and betrays a group or country.'),Q('traitor.q2','traitor.s1','context','A character betrays a friend’s trust for personal gain. What might the friend call them?','A traitor.','A trainee.','A trainer.','Betraying a friend can make someone a traitor.'),Q('traitor.q3','traitor.s1','distinction','Which action most clearly makes someone a traitor?','Handing secret military plans to the opposing country.','Following a marked trail through a forest.','Taking the last train home.','The first action betrays one’s country or side.'),Q('traitor.q4','traitor.s1','word-choice','Which phrase is natural?','a traitor to the cause','a traitor of teaching a skill','a traitor of carrying cargo','The construction “traitor to” identifies the group or cause betrayed.')]);
P('trajectory','From Latin trajectoria, a “course or path,” based on trans- “across” and iacere “to throw.”',[C('trajectory.s1','物理运动','The engineer calculated the rocket’s trajectory before launch.','工程師在發射前計算了火箭的運行軌跡。','the trajectory of + moving object','Noun: the curved path an object follows through space.','The calculation predicts the rocket’s path.'),C('trajectory.s2','发展趋势','After the policy changed, the city’s unemployment trajectory began to slope downward.','政策改變後，該市的失業率走勢開始下降。','a growth / career / economic trajectory','Noun: the course of development or change over time.','The trend describes how unemployment changes over a period.')],[M('The rocket’s trajectory was its final destination, not the path it followed through the sky.','The rocket’s trajectory was the curved path it followed through the sky.','Trajectory names a path or course, not simply the destination.')],[Q('trajectory.q1','trajectory.s1','meaning','What does a rocket’s trajectory describe?','The path it follows through space.','The person who trained its engineers.','The amount of fuel in a station.','The physical sense is the course followed by a moving object.'),Q('trajectory.q2','trajectory.s2','context','If a career trajectory improves, what is changing?','The person’s development or progress over time.','The exact curve of a rocket only.','A train is changing its track gauge.','Trajectory can mean a course of development.'),Q('trajectory.q3','trajectory.s1','distinction','Which use is about physical motion?','The ball’s trajectory curved toward the boundary.','The company’s growth trajectory rose for five years.','Her career trajectory changed after graduation.','The ball has a path through space.'),Q('trajectory.q4','trajectory.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses trajectory figuratively?','the downward trajectory of prices','the rocket’s trajectory through the atmosphere','the projectile’s curved trajectory','Prices follow a course of change over time.')]);
P('tram','First recorded in Scots and northern English for a rail wagon; the ultimate source is uncertain.',[C('tram.s1','城市交通','We took the tram across the city because traffic was slow.','因為交通緩慢，我們搭電車穿過市區。','take / catch a tram','Noun: an electric passenger vehicle running on rails in city streets.','The vehicle carries passengers along street-level rails.'),C('tram.s2','公共交通系统','The city is extending its tram to the university district.','該市正把電車系統延伸到大學區。','by tram / a city’s tram','Noun: a city’s system of such vehicles.','The announcement concerns the urban transit network.')],[M('We caught a tram on the motorway, where it flew above the traffic without rails.','We caught a tram on city tracks and rode it through the streets.','A tram runs on rails, commonly along urban streets.')],[Q('tram.q1','tram.s1','meaning','What kind of vehicle is a city tram?','An electric passenger vehicle running on rails in the street.','A film preview pulled behind a car.','A path of footprints left in mud.','The vehicle sense is an electric rail passenger vehicle.'),Q('tram.q2','tram.s2','context','If the city extends its tram, what is being expanded?','Its urban rail-transit system.','The length of a railway carriage.','A driver’s training course.','Tram can also refer to the city system using those vehicles.'),Q('tram.q3','tram.s1','distinction','Which journey is most likely by tram?','A ride between two downtown stops on street rails.','A flight from one continent to another.','A walk along a forest path.','Street-level rail transit is typical of a tram.'),Q('tram.q4','tram.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses tram for the system?','The tram serves six neighbourhoods.','She boarded one tram at the stop.','The tram’s trailer carried grain.','Serving neighbourhoods describes a transit system.')]);
P('trammel','From Middle English tramel, an old word for a net or restraint; historical derivation is uncertain.',[C('trammel.s1','限制','The permit process removed the legal trammels that had blocked small businesses.','許可程序消除了妨礙小企業發展的法律束縛。','trammels on / to + freedom or action','Noun: a restriction on freedom of action.','The rules had limited what businesses could do.'),C('trammel.s2','阻碍','Fear of public criticism trammelled the committee’s discussion.','對公眾批評的恐懼束縛了委員會的討論。','trammel + person, action, or progress','Verb: limit or hinder someone or something.','The fear prevented open discussion.')],[M('The committee said it was trammelled by rules, but the rules gave it complete freedom to act.','The committee was trammelled by rules that restricted its freedom to act.','To trammel is to restrict or hinder, not to give freedom.')],[Q('trammel.q1','trammel.s1','meaning','What are legal trammels on a business?','Restrictions that limit what it can do.','Rewards for training its staff.','Vehicles carrying goods by rail.','The noun sense is a restraint on freedom of action.'),Q('trammel.q2','trammel.s2','context','If fear trammels a committee, what happens?','Fear hinders or restricts its work.','Fear makes the committee’s work completely free.','Fear carries its members in a trailer.','The verb means to limit or hinder.'),Q('trammel.q3','trammel.s1','distinction','Which situation involves a trammel?','A rule prevents a group from discussing certain options.','A coach teaches runners new skills.','A tram follows tracks through town.','The rule is a restriction on the group’s action.'),Q('trammel.q4','trammel.s2','grammar','Choose the sentence using trammel as a verb.','The outdated rule trammelled the investigation.','The trammel of the contract was a legal restraint.','They boarded the trammel at the station.','“Trammelled the investigation” describes hindering it.')]);
P('tramp','A Germanic walking word of uncertain deeper origin; it is also used for a person who wanders without a home.',[C('tramp.s1','人物称呼','The old novel describes a tramp seeking shelter in a railway station.','那本舊小說描寫一名流浪者在火車站尋找庇護。','a tramp (historical / sometimes offensive)','Noun: a person who wanders from place to place without a home or job.','The character has no settled home.'),C('tramp.s2','徒步行走','We tramped across the moor for hours before finding the marked path.','我們在荒原上艱難地走了幾個小時，才找到有標記的小徑。','tramp through / across + area','Verb: walk heavily or for a long distance with effort.','The hikers cover rough ground on foot.')],[M('The hikers tramped across the moor without walking, using a train instead.','The hikers tramped across the moor on foot for several hours.','Tramp as a verb means to walk heavily or for a long distance.')],[Q('tramp.q1','tramp.s1','meaning','In the novel, who is a tramp?','A person wandering without a settled home or job.','A coach teaching a sport.','A rail vehicle carrying passengers.','The noun has a historical sense for a homeless wanderer.'),Q('tramp.q2','tramp.s2','context','What did the hikers do when they tramped across the moor?','They walked for a long distance over rough ground.','They rode in a city tram.','They stayed still in a dreamlike state.','The verb describes effortful walking.'),Q('tramp.q3','tramp.s1','distinction','Which use is the person noun?','A tramp asked for a place to sleep.','They tramp through mud all afternoon.','The boots tramp loudly along the path.','The first sentence names a person.'),Q('tramp.q4','tramp.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses tramp naturally as a verb?','They tramped through the snow to the cabin.','They trained the tramp through the snow.','They tramped the cabin as a person with no home.','The phrase describes strenuous walking through an area.')]);
P('trample','From tramp + frequentative -le, describing repeated heavy steps.',[C('trample.s1','践踏','Please stay on the path so visitors do not trample the seedlings.','請留在小徑上，免得遊客踩壞幼苗。','trample on / over + plants or ground','Verb: step heavily on something and crush or damage it.','Heavy steps would crush the young plants.'),C('trample.s2','侵犯权利','The court ruled that the policy trampled on workers’ privacy.','法院裁定該政策侵犯了工人的隱私。','trample on + rights or feelings','Verb: treat rights or feelings with disrespect.','The policy failed to respect the workers’ privacy.')],[M('The policy trampled on workers’ privacy because it carefully protected every personal record.','The policy trampled on workers’ privacy by exposing their personal records without consent.','Trample on privacy means violate or disrespect it, not protect it.')],[Q('trample.q1','trample.s1','meaning','What happens when visitors trample seedlings?','They step on and damage the young plants.','They train the seedlings for a race.','They leave the seedlings untouched.','The literal verb means step heavily on and crush.'),Q('trample.q2','trample.s2','context','What does it mean to trample on someone’s rights?','To disregard or violate those rights.','To protect the rights carefully.','To walk through a forest without a path.','The figurative sense concerns disrespect for rights or feelings.'),Q('trample.q3','trample.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses trample literally?','The crowd trampled the flower bed.','The law trampled on the residents’ freedoms.','The company trampled on the workers’ dignity.','The crowd physically stepped on flowers.'),Q('trample.q4','trample.s2','word-choice','Which phrase is figurative?','trample on a community’s dignity','trample the grass under heavy boots','trample fallen leaves along the path','Dignity is an abstract quality, so the phrase is figurative.')]);
P('trance','From Old French transe, related to Latin transire “to go across or pass.”',[C('trance.s1','意识状态','The rhythmic drumming left him in a trance, barely aware of the room.','有節奏的鼓聲使他進入恍惚狀態，幾乎沒有注意到房間。','fall / be in a trance','Noun: a dreamlike state in which someone barely notices surroundings.','He is absorbed and minimally aware of what is around him.'),C('trance.s2','高度专注','The dancers watched the lights in a trance of concentration.','舞者們極度專注地注視著燈光。','a trance of + attention or fascination','Noun: a state of intense interest that makes someone forget everything else.','Their fascination holds their attention completely.'),C('trance.s3','使入迷','The storyteller tranced the children with a vivid account of the voyage.','講故事的人用生動的航海故事讓孩子們聽得入迷。','trance + someone (rare verb)','Verb: put someone into a dreamlike or fascinated state.','The story absorbs the children.')],[M('He was in a trance, fully alert to every sound and detail around him.','He was in a trance, barely aware of the sounds around him.','A trance involves reduced awareness or intense absorption, not full alert attention.')],[Q('trance.q1','trance.s1','meaning','How aware is a person in a dreamlike trance?','They barely notice their surroundings.','They notice every detail more sharply than usual.','They are physically walking through a forest.','The first sense is a dreamlike state with little awareness.'),Q('trance.q2','trance.s2','context','Why did the dancers seem in a trance of concentration?','Their intense focus made them forget other things.','They were counting railway carriages.','They were speaking a transcript word for word.','Trance can describe intense fascination or absorption.'),Q('trance.q3','trance.s3','distinction','Which sentence uses trance as a verb?','The music tranced the audience into silence.','The audience fell into a trance.','She watched in a trance of fascination.','The first sentence uses the rare verb to mean fascinate or absorb.'),Q('trance.q4','trance.s1','word-choice','Which scene most clearly shows a trance?','He stared ahead after the long ritual and barely heard his name.','He carefully answered every question in a noisy room.','He walked briskly along a marked trail.','Reduced awareness of surroundings fits the dreamlike sense.')]);
P('tranquil','From Latin tranquillus, “quiet, calm, or undisturbed.”',[C('tranquil.s1','环境宁静','The cove was tranquil before the first boats crossed the water.','第一批船隻駛過水面前，這處小海灣十分寧靜。','a tranquil place / setting','Adjective: quiet and peaceful, without noise or activity.','The setting is still and calm.'),C('tranquil.s2','内心平静','After speaking with her doctor, she felt tranquil about the treatment.','和醫生談過後，她對治療感到安心平靜。','feel / remain tranquil','Adjective: free from worry or strong emotion.','Her worry has eased.')],[M('The tranquil cove was filled with shouting, crashing waves, and frantic activity.','The tranquil cove was quiet and undisturbed before the boats arrived.','A tranquil place is peaceful and quiet, not noisy and frantic.')],[Q('tranquil.q1','tranquil.s1','meaning','What is a tranquil cove like?','Quiet and peaceful, with little disturbance.','Crowded with noisy traffic.','Covered by a line of muddy footprints.','The place sense means calm and without noise or activity.'),Q('tranquil.q2','tranquil.s2','context','If she feels tranquil about treatment, how does she feel?','Calm and free from strong worry.','Angry and increasingly anxious.','Ready to board a freight train.','The mental sense is peace of mind.'),Q('tranquil.q3','tranquil.s1','distinction','Which scene is tranquil in the environmental sense?','A still garden before visitors arrive.','A packed station during a delay.','A loud crowd shouting at a match.','The quiet garden has little noise or activity.'),Q('tranquil.q4','tranquil.s2','word-choice','Which sentence uses tranquil for a state of mind?','He remained tranquil after hearing the reassuring news.','The tranquil lake had no boats.','A tranquil breeze crossed the garden.','Remaining calm after news describes someone’s emotional state.')]);
P('tranquility','From tranquil + -ity, naming the quality or state of being calm.',[C('tranquility.s1','环境安宁','The reserve protects the tranquility of the wetlands from traffic noise.','自然保護區保護濕地的寧靜，使其免受交通噪音干擾。','the tranquility of + place','Noun: calm quietness in a place without disturbance.','The protected place is peaceful and quiet.'),C('tranquility.s2','心境平和','She found a sense of tranquility while meditating beside the stream.','她在溪邊冥想時感受到內心平和。','a sense of / inner tranquility','Noun: a peaceful state of mind free from worry.','Meditation leaves her mentally calm.')],[M('The tranquility of the library was broken by hours of loud drilling and shouting.','The library’s tranquility came from its quiet rooms and lack of disturbance.','Tranquility is calm quietness, not prolonged loud noise.')],[Q('tranquility.q1','tranquility.s1','meaning','What does a reserve protect when it protects a wetland’s tranquility?','Its peaceful quietness and freedom from disturbance.','The wetland’s number of railway carriages.','A list of students’ grades.','The place sense names quietness without disturbance.'),Q('tranquility.q2','tranquility.s2','context','What might meditation give someone?','A peaceful state of mind.','A loud and crowded station.','A path of muddy footprints.','Inner tranquility means a calm mental state.'),Q('tranquility.q3','tranquility.s1','distinction','Which is an example of environmental tranquility?','A quiet garden with no traffic nearby.','A person feeling calm after a conversation.','A person learning a new job.','The garden’s lack of noise is environmental tranquility.'),Q('tranquility.q4','tranquility.s2','word-choice','Which phrase refers to a person’s mind?','a moment of inner tranquility','the tranquility of an empty beach','the tranquility of a quiet valley','“Inner” points to a peaceful state of mind.')]);
P('tranquilize','From tranquil + -ize; the verb means to make calm or give a sedative.',[C('tranquilize.s1','兽医与动物','The veterinarian tranquilized the injured fox before treating its leg.','獸醫先給受傷的狐狸使用鎮靜劑，再治療牠的腿。','tranquilize + person or animal','Verb: calm someone or administer a tranquillizer, especially to an animal.','The sedative makes the fox calm enough for treatment.')],[M('The veterinarian tranquilized the fox with a stimulant that made it more agitated.','The veterinarian tranquilized the fox with a sedative that calmed it.','To tranquilize is to calm or sedate, not stimulate or agitate.')],[Q('tranquilize.q1','tranquilize.s1','meaning','Why did the veterinarian tranquilize the fox?','To calm it so treatment could be given safely.','To make it more alert and aggressive.','To teach it how to follow a trail.','The verb means calm or sedate, often before an animal is handled.'),Q('tranquilize.q2','tranquilize.s1','context','What kind of drug would tranquilize an animal?','A sedative that reduces agitation.','A stimulant that increases agitation.','A medicine that records a transcript.','A tranquillizer calms or sedates.'),Q('tranquilize.q3','tranquilize.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses tranquilize correctly?','Rangers tranquilized the bear before moving it.','Rangers tranquilized the bear to make it run faster.','Rangers tranquilized the bear by shouting loudly.','Sedation allows the bear to be moved more safely.'),Q('tranquilize.q4','tranquilize.s1','grammar','Choose the natural object of tranquilize.','The vet tranquilized the nervous dog.','The vet tranquilized the dog’s training schedule.','The vet tranquilized a film trailer.','People and animals can be calmed or sedated.')]);
P('tranquilizer','From tranquilize + -er, naming a drug that reduces anxiety or causes sedation.',[C('tranquilizer.s1','药物','The doctor discussed the risks before prescribing a tranquilizer for severe anxiety.','醫生在為嚴重焦慮開鎮靜劑前先說明了風險。','take / prescribe a tranquilizer','Noun: a drug that calms anxiety or sedates, not necessarily causing sleep.','The medicine reduces anxiety; it is not described as a sleeping pill.')],[M('The label called the tranquilizer an energy booster that increases anxiety and agitation.','The label described the tranquilizer as a medicine that reduces anxiety.','A tranquilizer calms rather than heightens anxiety or stimulation.')],[Q('tranquilizer.q1','tranquilizer.s1','meaning','What is a tranquilizer prescribed for severe anxiety intended to do?','Reduce anxiety or calm the patient.','Increase agitation and alertness.','Treat a broken rail line.','A tranquilizer is a drug that calms anxiety or sedates.'),Q('tranquilizer.q2','tranquilizer.s1','context','Does every tranquilizer necessarily make a person sleep?','No; it can reduce anxiety without inducing sleep.','Yes; it is always a strong sleeping drug.','No; it is a type of sports shoe.','The sense specifies calming or sedation without requiring sleep.'),Q('tranquilizer.q3','tranquilizer.s1','distinction','Which item is a tranquilizer?','A medicine used to reduce severe anxiety.','A device that sends radio signals.','A soft shoe worn at the gym.','The medicine is used for its calming effect.'),Q('tranquilizer.q4','tranquilizer.s1','word-choice','Which phrase is most accurate?','a prescribed tranquilizer to ease anxiety','a tranquilizer to make the patient more agitated','a tranquilizer that is necessarily a train ticket','The drug is prescribed to calm anxiety, not intensify it.')]);
P('tranquilliser','British spelling of tranquilizer, formed from tranquillise + -er.',[C('tranquilliser.s1','药物','Her doctor explained how the prescribed tranquilliser could reduce acute anxiety.','醫生向她說明處方鎮靜劑如何減輕急性焦慮。','a tranquilliser for anxiety','Noun: a drug that reduces tension or sedates a person or animal.','The medicine is prescribed to calm anxiety.')],[M('The clinic gave him a tranquilliser to increase his anxiety and keep him agitated.','The clinic gave him a tranquilliser to reduce his anxiety and calm him.','A tranquilliser is used to reduce tension or sedate, not intensify anxiety.')],[Q('tranquilliser.q1','tranquilliser.s1','meaning','Why might a doctor prescribe a tranquilliser?','To reduce tension or calm a patient.','To make a patient more agitated.','To transport the patient by rail.','The medicine is used to reduce tension or sedate.'),Q('tranquilliser.q2','tranquilliser.s1','context','Which spelling is commonly used in British English?','tranquilliser','trancecarriage','tranquilest','Tranquilliser is the British spelling of the noun.'),Q('tranquilliser.q3','tranquilliser.s1','distinction','Which item is a tranquilliser?','A prescribed medicine that eases acute anxiety.','A trainer who coaches a runner.','A short preview of a film.','The medicine is the calming drug.'),Q('tranquilliser.q4','tranquilliser.s1','word-choice','Which phrase is semantically correct?','a tranquilliser prescribed to calm the patient','a tranquilliser prescribed to raise tension','a tranquilliser used as a train timetable','The phrase matches the drug’s calming purpose.')]);
P('tranquillity','Variant spelling of tranquility, from tranquil + -ity.',[C('tranquillity.s1','环境宁静','The remote garden offered tranquillity away from traffic and construction.','這座偏遠花園遠離交通與施工，帶來寧靜。','the tranquillity of + place','Noun: the quality of being quiet, still, and free from disturbance.','The garden is calm because noise and activity are absent.')],[M('The tranquillity of the garden came from constant construction noise and heavy traffic.','The tranquillity of the garden came from its stillness and distance from traffic.','Tranquillity means quietness and freedom from disturbance.')],[Q('tranquillity.q1','tranquillity.s1','meaning','What did the remote garden offer?','Quietness and freedom from disturbance.','A crowded railway platform.','A course for new gardeners.','The noun means calm stillness without disturbance.'),Q('tranquillity.q2','tranquillity.s1','context','Why might someone seek the tranquillity of a country retreat?','To get away from noise and activity.','To hear construction more clearly.','To watch a film preview.','A tranquil place is quiet and undisturbed.'),Q('tranquillity.q3','tranquillity.s1','distinction','Which scene has tranquillity?','A still garden far from traffic.','A packed tram rattling through a busy street.','A crowd shouting at a concert.','The garden has the quietness associated with tranquillity.'),Q('tranquillity.q4','tranquillity.s1','word-choice','Choose the phrase that fits.','the tranquillity of the mountain lake','the tranquillity of a siren-filled street','the tranquillity of a noisy factory floor','The quiet lake setting supports the meaning of the noun.')]);
P('transact','From Latin transigere, “to carry through or accomplish,” formed from trans- and agere “do.”',[C('transact.s1','商务事务','The two firms transact business through a secure online portal.','兩家公司透過安全的線上平台辦理業務。','transact business / a deal','Verb: carry out business or official matters formally.','The firms conduct their commercial affairs.'),C('transact.s2','买卖协商','Local farmers transact directly with restaurants at the weekly market.','當地農民在每週市集直接與餐廳交易。','transact with + buyer or seller','Verb: buy and sell, or reach an agreement through dealings.','The farmers and restaurants conduct trade with each other.')],[M('The firms transacted business by refusing to communicate or complete any agreement.','The firms transacted business through a secure portal and completed their agreement.','To transact business is to conduct or complete business dealings.')],[Q('transact.q1','transact.s1','meaning','What do two firms do when they transact business?','They formally conduct commercial matters.','They follow a path through a forest.','They change a text into another language.','The verb means carry out business or official matters.'),Q('transact.q2','transact.s2','context','Farmers transact directly with restaurants. What happens?','They buy, sell, or agree on trade with one another.','They teach restaurant staff to drive a tram.','They send a radio signal to a restaurant.','The trade sense involves dealings between parties.'),Q('transact.q3','transact.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses transact for formal business?','The bank transacts payments for its clients.','The hikers transact across the ridge.','The editor transacts a poem into French.','Processing payments is conducting business.'),Q('transact.q4','transact.s2','grammar','Which construction is natural for the trade sense?','The cooperative transacted with local suppliers.','The cooperative transacted at the mountain path.','The cooperative transacted the supplier into a poem.','“Transact with” can describe buying, selling, or dealing with another party.')]);
P('transaction','From transact + -ion, naming a business deal or the process of carrying one out.',[C('transaction.s1','金融交易','The card company flagged the transaction because the purchase came from abroad.','這筆購物來自國外，因此信用卡公司標記了該交易。','record / approve a transaction','Noun: a business deal in which money or goods change hands.','A purchase is recorded as a commercial exchange.'),C('transaction.s2','操作过程','The database saves each transaction before confirming the order.','資料庫會在確認訂單前儲存每次操作。','process / complete a transaction','Noun: the process of doing business or carrying out a computer operation.','The database records an operation in the order system.')],[M('The bank recorded a transaction even though no money or goods changed hands and no operation occurred.','The bank recorded the transaction when the customer paid for the goods.','A transaction is a business exchange or a completed operation.')],[Q('transaction.q1','transaction.s1','meaning','What is a purchase transaction?','A business exchange involving payment for goods.','A person learning to perform a job.','A vehicle carrying freight.','The first sense is a deal where money or goods change hands.'),Q('transaction.q2','transaction.s2','context','Why does a database save a transaction before confirming an order?','It records the operation being carried out.','It records a film preview.','It records the curve of a moving object.','Transaction can mean a computer operation.'),Q('transaction.q3','transaction.s1','distinction','Which is a commercial transaction?','A customer pays a shop for a bicycle.','A computer copies DNA into RNA.','A train follows its route to a city.','Payment for goods is a business deal.'),Q('transaction.q4','transaction.s2','word-choice','Which phrase refers to a computer operation?','Each transaction is stored in the database log.','A cash transaction took place at the shop.','The transaction of the parcel took three days.','The database log records individual operations.')]);
P('transcend','From Latin transcendere, “to climb or go beyond,” from trans- + scandere.',[C('transcend.s1','界限与语言','The film’s appeal transcends language because viewers understand its emotions without dialogue.','這部電影的感染力超越了語言，觀眾即使沒有對白也能理解其中情感。','transcend + limit or category','Verb: go beyond a normal limit or boundary.','Its appeal reaches beyond a language barrier.'),C('transcend.s2','超越比较','Her commitment to the community transcended personal ambition.','她對社區的投入超越了個人抱負。','transcend + something in importance','Verb: be greater or more important than something else.','Community service mattered more than her own advancement.')],[M('The film transcended language because viewers could understand it only after learning every line of dialogue.','The film transcended language because its visual story was clear without spoken dialogue.','To transcend language is to go beyond the need for a shared language.')],[Q('transcend.q1','transcend.s1','meaning','If a story transcends language, what does it do?','It communicates beyond the limits of a shared language.','It becomes a written transcript.','It stays within one vocabulary only.','The verb can mean go beyond a limit or boundary.'),Q('transcend.q2','transcend.s2','context','Her commitment transcended personal ambition. What mattered more?','Serving the community mattered more than her own advancement.','Her promotion mattered more than the community.','She could no longer understand the language.','The comparison sense means be greater or more important.'),Q('transcend.q3','transcend.s1','distinction','Which use is about going beyond a boundary?','The melody transcended cultural divisions.','Her effort transcended his in importance.','The team transcribed the melody for piano.','Crossing cultural divisions fits the boundary sense.'),Q('transcend.q4','transcend.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses transcend to compare importance?','The public interest transcended the minister’s convenience.','The bridge transcended the river physically.','The subtitle transcended a spoken sentence into text.','The sentence says public interest was more important.')]);
P('transcendent','From Latin transcendentem, present participle of transcendere “to go beyond.”',[C('transcendent.s1','艺术体验','The final movement created a transcendent calm that seemed to lift the audience beyond ordinary experience.','最後樂章營造出超凡的平靜，彷彿使觀眾超越了日常經驗。','a transcendent experience / quality','Adjective: surpassing ordinary experience or standards; in philosophy, beyond the material world.','The music feels beyond everyday experience.')],[M('The dull routine was called transcendent even though it was entirely ordinary and did not exceed any standard.','The performance felt transcendent because it surpassed ordinary experience.','Transcendent describes something that goes beyond ordinary experience or standards.')],[Q('transcendent.q1','transcendent.s1','meaning','What kind of experience is transcendent?','One that seems to surpass ordinary experience.','One that is entirely routine and unremarkable.','One that lists course grades.','The adjective describes something beyond ordinary experience or standards.'),Q('transcendent.q2','transcendent.s1','context','Why might a listener call a performance transcendent?','It feels extraordinary and beyond everyday experience.','It is exactly like a routine announcement.','It contains no music or sound.','A transcendent experience seems to rise above the ordinary.'),Q('transcendent.q3','transcendent.s1','distinction','Which description best fits a transcendent moment?','A powerful moment that feels beyond normal life.','A routine task repeated in the usual way.','A temporary delay on a bus route.','The first description surpasses ordinary experience.'),Q('transcendent.q4','transcendent.s1','word-choice','Which phrase uses transcendent naturally?','a transcendent sense of peace','a transcendent list of ordinary office supplies','a transcendent train timetable with no unusual quality','The phrase names an unusually elevated experience.')]);
P('transcendental','From transcendental, used in philosophy for what concerns conditions beyond ordinary experience; popularized in English through Kantian philosophy.',[C('transcendental.s1','哲学','Kant’s transcendental argument asks what conditions make experience and knowledge possible.','康德的先驗論證探討哪些條件使經驗與知識成為可能。','transcendental + argument / philosophy','Adjective: going beyond limits of ordinary experience; in Kant, concerning conditions that make knowledge possible.','The argument examines the preconditions of knowing.')],[M('The essay called its list of daily grocery prices a transcendental argument about the conditions of knowledge.','The essay presented a transcendental argument about the conditions that make knowledge possible.','In Kantian use, transcendental concerns conditions for the possibility of knowledge, not an ordinary list.')],[Q('transcendental.q1','transcendental.s1','meaning','What does a Kantian transcendental argument examine?','Conditions that make experience or knowledge possible.','The daily price of every grocery item.','The route a train follows through space.','The philosophical sense concerns preconditions of knowledge.'),Q('transcendental.q2','transcendental.s1','context','Why is the question “How is experience possible?” called transcendental here?','It asks about conditions underlying knowledge.','It asks how to transcribe a speech.','It asks how much a train can carry.','Kantian transcendental inquiry studies conditions that make knowledge possible.'),Q('transcendental.q3','transcendental.s1','distinction','Which topic is most clearly transcendental philosophy?','The conditions that allow any experience to be known.','A record of one person’s grocery bill.','A physical path of a rocket.','The first topic concerns the possibility of knowledge.'),Q('transcendental.q4','transcendental.s1','word-choice','Choose the phrase that fits the philosophical sense.','a transcendental inquiry into the grounds of knowledge','a transcendental receipt for daily purchases','a transcendental timetable for a city tram','The philosophical inquiry asks what makes knowledge possible.')]);
P('transcontinental','A compound of trans- “across” and continental, from continent.',[C('transcontinental.s1','交通与地理','The transcontinental railway linked the Atlantic coast with cities on the Pacific.','這條橫貫大陸的鐵路連接大西洋沿岸與太平洋沿岸的城市。','transcontinental + route, railway, or journey','Adjective: extending or travelling across a whole continent.','The railway crosses the continent from coast to coast.')],[M('The short local tram line was called transcontinental although it never left one neighbourhood.','The transcontinental railway crossed the continent from one coast to the other.','Transcontinental describes something extending or travelling across a continent.')],[Q('transcontinental.q1','transcontinental.s1','meaning','What does a transcontinental railway do?','It extends across a whole continent.','It serves one block of a city only.','It carries a film preview behind a car.','The prefix trans- signals crossing; the adjective refers to a continent.'),Q('transcontinental.q2','transcontinental.s1','context','A transcontinental journey runs from the Atlantic to the Pacific. How far does it go?','Across the continent from one coast to another.','Around one city neighbourhood.','Between two platforms at one station.','The journey crosses a whole continent.'),Q('transcontinental.q3','transcontinental.s1','distinction','Which project is transcontinental?','A railway connecting distant coasts across a continent.','A tram route connecting two downtown stops.','A footpath through one park.','The coast-to-coast railway crosses a continent.'),Q('transcontinental.q4','transcontinental.s1','word-choice','Which phrase is most natural?','a transcontinental flight across Asia','a transcontinental path across one room','a transcontinental stop at the next street corner','The flight spans an entire continent.')]);
P('transcribe','From Latin transcribere, “to write across or copy,” from trans- + scribere.',[C('transcribe.s1','语音转写','The assistant transcribed the interview from the audio recording.','助理根據錄音把訪談逐字轉寫下來。','transcribe speech / an interview','Verb: write down speech from a recording word for word.','The spoken interview becomes written text.'),C('transcribe.s2','音乐与符号','The arranger transcribed the violin melody for a small brass ensemble.','編曲者把小提琴旋律改編為小型銅管樂合奏。','transcribe music for + instruments','Verb: arrange music for different instruments or represent sounds in symbols.','The melody is written for a different group of instruments.')],[M('The assistant transcribed the interview by deleting every spoken word and leaving no written copy.','The assistant transcribed the interview by writing down the spoken words from the recording.','To transcribe speech is to make a written copy of it.')],[Q('transcribe.q1','transcribe.s1','meaning','What does an assistant do when transcribing an interview?','Writes down the spoken words from its recording.','Changes a violin melody into a brass arrangement.','Moves an employee to another department.','The speech sense means write down recorded words.'),Q('transcribe.q2','transcribe.s2','context','What happened when the melody was transcribed for brass?','It was arranged or written for different instruments.','It was deleted without being written.','It was carried on a railway.','The music sense involves arranging for another instrument group.'),Q('transcribe.q3','transcribe.s1','distinction','Which example is speech transcription?','Typing every word from a recorded interview.','Changing a song into another key.','Pointing a camera at a stage.','Typing recorded speech creates a written transcript.'),Q('transcribe.q4','transcribe.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses transcribe in its music sense?','transcribe a piano piece for a string quartet','transcribe a meeting from its audio file','transcribe a student to another college','The first phrase adapts music for different instruments.')]);
P('transcript','From Latin transcriptum, “something copied,” the past participle of transcribere.',[C('transcript.s1','会议记录','The journalist checked the transcript against the interview recording.','記者對照訪談錄音核對文字稿。','a transcript of + speech or interview','Noun: a written copy of what was said.','The text records spoken words.'),C('transcript.s2','教育记录','The scholarship office requested an official transcript of her university grades.','獎學金辦公室要求她提供正式的大學成績單。','an academic transcript','Noun: an official list of a student’s courses and grades.','The document lists coursework and results.')],[M('The university transcript listed only the student’s favourite quotations, not courses or grades.','The university transcript listed the student’s courses and grades.','An academic transcript is an official record of coursework and results.')],[Q('transcript.q1','transcript.s1','meaning','What does an interview transcript contain?','A written record of what the speakers said.','A list of university grades only.','A path followed by a rocket.','The first sense is a written copy of speech.'),Q('transcript.q2','transcript.s2','context','Why did the scholarship office request an official transcript?','To review the student’s courses and grades.','To see a preview of an upcoming film.','To learn the railway route.','An academic transcript lists courses and results.'),Q('transcript.q3','transcript.s1','distinction','Which document is a speech transcript?','A typed copy of a recorded interview.','A certified list of a student’s marks.','A ticket that cannot be transferred.','The first document copies spoken words.'),Q('transcript.q4','transcript.s2','word-choice','Which phrase is natural for university records?','request an academic transcript','transcribe a transcript of the grades','ride an academic transcript','A transcript is the official document of courses and grades.')]);
P('transcription','From Latin transcriptio, from transcribere “to copy or write across.”',[C('transcription.s1','访谈文字稿','The transcription of the hearing was checked for errors before publication.','聽證會的文字記錄在發布前經過了錯誤核對。','transcription of + speech or meeting','Noun: the act of writing a copy or the written copy itself.','The hearing’s spoken record has been converted into text.'),C('transcription.s2','分子生物学','In the cell, transcription copies a DNA sequence into RNA.','在細胞中，轉錄會把 DNA 序列複製成 RNA。','DNA transcription into RNA','Noun: the cellular process of copying DNA information into RNA.','The molecule being produced is RNA, copied from DNA.')],[M('During transcription, the cell copies RNA into DNA to make the original sequence.','During transcription, the cell copies a DNA sequence into RNA.','In the source’s biological sense, DNA is copied into RNA.')],[Q('transcription.q1','transcription.s1','meaning','What is a transcription of a hearing?','A written copy of the spoken proceedings.','A list of a student’s course grades.','A vehicle that carries goods.','The general sense is the act or result of writing out speech.'),Q('transcription.q2','transcription.s2','context','In cellular transcription, what is copied into RNA?','A DNA sequence.','A transcript of a university course.','A radio signal into a film preview.','The biological process copies DNA information into RNA.'),Q('transcription.q3','transcription.s1','distinction','Which example is not biological transcription?','Typing the spoken words from a public hearing.','A cell making RNA from DNA.','A laboratory measuring RNA production.','Writing spoken words is the general copy-making sense.'),Q('transcription.q4','transcription.s2','word-choice','Which phrase fits molecular biology?','DNA transcription into RNA','a transcript of a student’s grades','the transcription of a radio interview','The DNA-to-RNA process is the biological sense.')]);
P('transfer','From Latin transferre, “to carry across,” formed from trans- + ferre.',[C('transfer.s1','移动与转移','The hospital transferred the patient to a specialist unit nearby.','醫院把病人轉送到附近的專科病房。','transfer someone / something to + place','Verb: move a person or thing from one place, person, or use to another.','The patient is moved to another location.'),C('transfer.s2','工作或学校','After two years, Mina transferred to a university closer to home.','兩年後，米娜轉到離家更近的大學就讀。','transfer to + school / team / job','Verb: move to a different job, school, or team.','She changes institutions.'),C('transfer.s3','换乘','Passengers must make a transfer at Central Station.','乘客必須在中央車站換乘。','make a transfer / a transfer at + station','Noun: an act of moving, or a change from one vehicle to another.','The journey includes a change of vehicle.')],[M('Mina transferred to the nearby university but stayed enrolled at her old school only.','Mina transferred to the nearby university and changed institutions.','Transfer to another university means move to that school, not remain enrolled at the old one.')],[Q('transfer.q1','transfer.s1','meaning','What happened when the hospital transferred the patient?','The patient was moved to another unit.','The patient received a list of course grades.','The patient was taught to operate a tram.','The first verb sense is moving someone or something to another place.'),Q('transfer.q2','transfer.s2','context','Mina transferred to a different university. What changed?','She moved to another school.','She changed trains at a station only.','She translated her coursework into English.','The school sense means move to another institution.'),Q('transfer.q3','transfer.s3','distinction','What does a transfer at Central Station mean for passengers?','They change vehicles during the journey.','They receive a degree transcript.','They train the station staff.','A transfer can be a change from one vehicle to another.'),Q('transfer.q4','transfer.s1','word-choice','Which sentence uses transfer for moving an item?','The lab transferred the samples to a colder room.','The student transferred to a new college.','We made a transfer between two trains.','The samples are moved to another place.')]);
P('transferable','From transfer + -able, meaning capable of being transferred.',[C('transferable.s1','票券与权利','The airline issued a transferable voucher that another passenger could use.','航空公司發出一張可轉讓的代用券，其他乘客也能使用。','transferable + ticket, voucher, right, or skill','Adjective: capable of being moved or passed to another person or use.','The voucher can be given to another passenger.')],[M('The voucher was transferable, but the rules said it could never be given or reassigned to anyone else.','The voucher was transferable, so its holder could give it to another passenger.','Transferable means capable of being transferred to another person or use.')],[Q('transferable.q1','transferable.s1','meaning','What does a transferable voucher allow?','It can be passed to another person.','It can never be reassigned.','It must be used to train an airline pilot.','The suffix -able means the voucher is capable of transfer.'),Q('transferable.q2','transferable.s1','context','If a skill is transferable, what can happen?','It can be useful in a different job or setting.','It must remain in one workplace forever.','It can only be printed as a transcript.','A transferable skill can be carried into another context.'),Q('transferable.q3','transferable.s1','distinction','Which item is explicitly transferable in the example?','A voucher another passenger may use.','An unassignable personal ticket.','A non-movable tram platform.','The voucher is allowed to pass to another user.'),Q('transferable.q4','transferable.s1','word-choice','Which sentence uses transferable correctly?','The contract gives her a transferable right to the licence.','The contract says her right is transferable because nobody else can receive it.','The contract calls the train transferable to a transcript.','A transferable right can be passed or assigned.')]);
P('transfix','From Latin transfigere, “to pierce through,” from trans- + figere “fasten.”',[C('transfix.s1','刺穿','The arrow transfixed the wooden target near its centre.','箭矢射穿了木製標靶接近中心的位置。','transfix + object with a sharp point','Verb: pierce through with a sharp object.','The arrow passes through the target.'),C('transfix.s2','惊呆与入迷','The sudden announcement transfixed the audience in stunned silence.','突如其來的公告使觀眾震驚得一動不動。','be / stand transfixed by + shock or sight','Verb: make someone unable to move with shock or fear.','Shock leaves the audience momentarily motionless.')],[M('The announcement transfixed the audience, who immediately ran around the hall without stopping.','The announcement transfixed the audience, leaving them motionless in shock.','Figurative transfix means make someone unable to move with shock or fear.')],[Q('transfix.q1','transfix.s1','meaning','What happened when the arrow transfixed the target?','It pierced through the target.','It calmed the target without touching it.','It carried the target to another place.','The literal sense is pierce with a sharp object.'),Q('transfix.q2','transfix.s2','context','Why did the audience stand transfixed after the announcement?','Shock left them unable to move.','They were calmly training for a race.','They were changing trains.','The figurative sense means immobilized by shock or fear.'),Q('transfix.q3','transfix.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses transfix literally?','The spear transfixed the shield.','The terrifying sight transfixed her.','The news left him transfixed.','The spear physically pierces through the shield.'),Q('transfix.q4','transfix.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses the emotional sense?','She stood transfixed with fear.','The nail transfixed the board.','The arrow transfixed the target.','Fear can leave a person unable to move.')]);
P('transform','From Latin transformare, “to change form,” from trans- + formare.',[C('transform.s1','彻底改变','The restoration project transformed the abandoned station into a lively arts centre.','修復計畫把廢棄車站改造成熱鬧的藝術中心。','transform + object into + new form','Verb: change the form, appearance, or character of something completely.','The station’s function and appearance change greatly.'),C('transform.s2','生物变化','A caterpillar transforms into a butterfly during its life cycle.','毛毛蟲在生命週期中會變成蝴蝶。','transform into + different form','Verb: change into a different form.','The organism becomes a different form.')],[M('The renovation transformed the station, leaving every room and its use exactly unchanged.','The renovation transformed the station into a lively arts centre.','To transform something is to change its form, appearance, or character.')],[Q('transform.q1','transform.s1','meaning','How did the project transform the station?','It changed the abandoned building into an arts centre.','It left the building and its use unchanged.','It copied the station into a transcript.','The first sense is to change something completely.'),Q('transform.q2','transform.s2','context','What happens when a caterpillar transforms into a butterfly?','It changes into a different form.','It moves to a different university.','It carries a load behind a car.','The second sense describes changing into another form.'),Q('transform.q3','transform.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses transform with an object?','The renovation transformed the old warehouse.','The caterpillar transformed into a butterfly.','The weather transformed overnight.','The renovation acts on the warehouse as its object.'),Q('transform.q4','transform.s2','word-choice','Which phrase describes a change into another form?','transform into a butterfly','transform a transcript for filing','transform the station with new paint','The phrase “into a butterfly” names the resulting form.')]);
P('transformation','From transform + -ation, naming a major change or a mathematical operation.',[C('transformation.s1','社会变化','The transformation of the mining town began when the old pits became parks.','舊礦坑改建為公園後，這座礦業小鎮開始轉型。','the transformation of + person, place, or system','Noun: a change that makes something very different from before.','The town changes in function and appearance.'),C('transformation.s2','数学','A rotation is a geometric transformation that turns a figure around a point.','旋轉是一種幾何變換，會使圖形繞著一個點轉動。','a geometric transformation','Noun: a mathematical rule or operation that changes a shape, value, or equation.','The operation changes the figure’s position.')],[M('The town’s transformation left its buildings, purpose, and appearance entirely unchanged.','The town’s transformation changed the former mining area into parks and public spaces.','A transformation is a change that makes something substantially different.')],[Q('transformation.q1','transformation.s1','meaning','What does the town’s transformation describe?','A major change in what the town looks like or how it functions.','A transcript of residents’ interviews only.','A temporary train transfer.','The general sense is a change making something very different.'),Q('transformation.q2','transformation.s2','context','What does a geometric transformation do to a figure?','Applies an operation that changes its position or form.','Lists a student’s course grades.','Copies DNA information into RNA.','The mathematical sense is an operation on a shape or value.'),Q('transformation.q3','transformation.s1','distinction','Which use is about social change rather than mathematics?','The transformation of the port into a public park.','A rotation as a geometric transformation.','A translation operation on a figure.','Changing a port into a park is a large real-world change.'),Q('transformation.q4','transformation.s2','word-choice','Which phrase names the mathematical sense?','a geometric transformation of a triangle','the transformation of a former factory into homes','the transformation of a town after a new railway','The triangle undergoes a mathematical operation.')]);
P('transfuse','From Latin transfundere, “to pour across,” from trans- + fundere.',[C('transfuse.s1','医疗','The team transfused two units of blood after the patient lost a dangerous amount.','病人失血嚴重後，醫療團隊輸入了兩單位的血液。','transfuse blood / fluid into + patient','Verb: pass blood or another fluid into a person’s circulation.','The blood enters the patient’s bloodstream.')],[M('The team transfused blood by removing it from the patient and never putting any fluid into the circulation.','The team transfused blood by passing it into the patient’s circulation.','To transfuse blood is to introduce it into the bloodstream.')],[Q('transfuse.q1','transfuse.s1','meaning','What does a medical team do when it transfuses blood?','Introduces blood into a patient’s circulation.','Copies a speech into written text.','Moves a passenger between trains.','The medical verb means pass blood or fluid into the circulation.'),Q('transfuse.q2','transfuse.s1','context','Why might a patient be transfused after heavy blood loss?','To replace blood by putting it into the circulation.','To remove all remaining blood.','To change the patient’s school.','A transfusion supplies blood to the patient.'),Q('transfuse.q3','transfuse.s1','distinction','Which action is transfusing?','A clinician gives a patient blood through an IV line.','A clerk writes down an interview.','A biologist copies DNA into RNA.','The IV introduces blood into the bloodstream.'),Q('transfuse.q4','transfuse.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural object of transfuse.','The hospital transfused blood into the patient.','The hospital transfused a transcript into a train.','The hospital transfused the patient to another school.','Blood or another fluid is what a clinician transfuses.')]);
P('transfusion','From Latin transfusio, from transfundere “to pour across.”',[C('transfusion.s1','医疗','A transfusion replaced some of the blood she had lost during surgery.','輸血補充了她在手術中流失的部分血液。','a blood transfusion','Noun: medical introduction of blood or another fluid into the bloodstream.','Blood is introduced into the patient’s circulation.')],[M('The transfusion removed blood from her body without introducing any blood or fluid.','The transfusion introduced donated blood into her bloodstream.','A transfusion is the medical introduction of blood or another fluid into the circulation.')],[Q('transfusion.q1','transfusion.s1','meaning','What is a blood transfusion?','The medical introduction of blood into the bloodstream.','The removal of all blood without replacement.','A written record of a speech.','A transfusion passes blood or fluid into the circulation.'),Q('transfusion.q2','transfusion.s1','context','Why did the patient receive a transfusion after surgery?','To replace blood she had lost.','To change the order of two columns.','To travel across a continent.','A transfusion can replace lost blood.'),Q('transfusion.q3','transfusion.s1','distinction','Which event is a transfusion?','Donated blood is given to a patient through a medical line.','A student receives an official grade record.','A radio signal is broadcast to another region.','The first is a medical introduction of blood.'),Q('transfusion.q4','transfusion.s1','word-choice','Which phrase is natural?','a transfusion of blood after the operation','a transfusion of railway carriages','a transfusion that writes an interview word for word','Blood is the fluid introduced during this medical procedure.')]);
P('transgress','From Latin transgredi, “to step across or go beyond,” from trans- + gradi.',[C('transgress.s1','规则','Visitors who transgress the laboratory rules may lose access to the facility.','違反實驗室規則的訪客可能會失去進入設施的資格。','transgress a law / rule / agreement','Verb: break a law, rule, or agreement.','The visitors violate rules governing the lab.'),C('transgress.s2','道德与宗教规范','The story follows a knight who transgresses the moral code he once defended.','故事講述一名騎士違背了自己曾捍衛的道德準則。','transgress a moral or religious code','Verb: go beyond what a moral or religious code permits.','The knight acts against the code’s limits.')],[M('The visitors transgressed the rules by following every requirement exactly.','The visitors transgressed the rules by entering the restricted laboratory.','To transgress a rule is to break or violate it, not obey it.')],[Q('transgress.q1','transgress.s1','meaning','What did visitors do if they transgressed the lab rules?','They broke or violated them.','They followed every requirement.','They recorded the rules as a transcript.','The first sense means break a rule or agreement.'),Q('transgress.q2','transgress.s2','context','What does it mean that the knight transgressed his moral code?','He acted beyond or against what the code permits.','He taught the code to a trainee.','He translated the code into another language.','The moral sense is to go beyond what a code allows.'),Q('transgress.q3','transgress.s1','distinction','Which is a transgression of a formal rule?','Entering a restricted lab without permission.','Reading the rules before entering.','Receiving permission from the supervisor.','Unauthorized entry breaks the lab rule.'),Q('transgress.q4','transgress.s2','word-choice','Which phrase best fits the moral sense?','transgress the ethical limits of the experiment','transgress the train’s schedule by arriving on time','transgress a transcript into another language','Ethical limits are a moral code one can violate.')]);
P('transient','From Latin transientem, “passing across or away,” present participle of transire.',[C('transient.s1','短暂变化','The relief from pain was transient, lasting only until the medicine wore off.','疼痛的緩解是短暫的，只持續到藥效消退。','transient + feeling, effect, or condition','Adjective: lasting for only a short time.','The relief soon disappears.'),C('transient.s2','短暂停留','The hostel provides simple rooms for transient workers on short contracts.','這家旅舍為短期合約的流動工人提供簡單房間。','transient + guest / population / worker','Adjective: staying or working in a place only temporarily.','The workers stay for a limited period.'),C('transient.s3','流动人员','The shelter offers meals to transients during the winter.','這家收容所冬季為暫居者提供餐食。','transients (people passing through)','Noun: a person who stays in a place for only a short time.','The people do not have a permanent stay in the area.')],[M('The transient relief lasted permanently and never faded after the medicine wore off.','The transient relief lasted only briefly before the pain returned.','Transient means temporary or short-lived, not permanent.')],[Q('transient.q1','transient.s1','meaning','What does transient relief mean?','Relief that lasts only a short time.','Relief that lasts forever.','Relief that transfers someone to a new school.','The adjective means lasting briefly.'),Q('transient.q2','transient.s2','context','Why are workers on short contracts called transient workers?','They stay or work in the place temporarily.','They are permanent residents for life.','They are people who copy interviews.','This sense describes temporary residence or employment.'),Q('transient.q3','transient.s3','distinction','Who are transients at a winter shelter?','People staying in the area only for a short time.','Staff who train new nurses.','People who permanently own the building.','The noun refers to people who are temporarily in a place.'),Q('transient.q4','transient.s1','word-choice','Which phrase uses transient for duration?','a transient improvement that soon disappeared','a permanent condition unchanged for decades','a resident who lives there permanently','The improvement is short-lived, matching transient.')]);
P('transistor','Coined from transfer + resistor for an electronic component that controls current; the word was introduced in the 1940s.',[C('transistor.s1','电子学','The tiny transistor switches current inside the calculator’s processor.','這個小電晶體在計算器處理器內切換電流。','a transistor in an electronic circuit','Noun: a small electronic component that controls the flow of electric current.','The component regulates current in the device.'),C('transistor.s2','便携收音机','Grandfather kept a transistor by the bed to listen to late-night news.','祖父把一台晶體管收音機放在床邊聽深夜新聞。','a transistor (informal, older radio sense)','Noun: a small portable radio using transistors.','The word stands for the compact radio itself.')],[M('The technician removed a transistor, which was a large acoustic drum used to amplify current.','The technician replaced the transistor, a small component that controls electric current.','A transistor is an electronic component, not an acoustic instrument.')],[Q('transistor.q1','transistor.s1','meaning','What does a transistor control in a circuit?','The flow of electric current.','The direction of a hiking trail.','The grades listed on a transcript.','The component regulates or switches electrical current.'),Q('transistor.q2','transistor.s2','context','What did Grandfather keep by the bed to hear the news?','A small portable radio called a transistor.','A tiny current-controlling part by itself.','A tram ticket.','Transistor can informally name a portable radio using transistors.'),Q('transistor.q3','transistor.s1','distinction','Which use refers to an electronic part?','The circuit contains a transistor that switches current.','He tuned his transistor to the news station.','She carried a transistor radio on the trip.','The first sentence describes a component inside a circuit.'),Q('transistor.q4','transistor.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses the older portable-radio sense?','She listened to a transistor while walking.','A transistor controlled the current on the circuit board.','The transistor was soldered inside the calculator.','Listening to one suggests the portable radio meaning.')]);
P('transit','From Latin transitus, “a going across or passage,” from transire.',[C('transit.s1','运输过程','The vaccines remained cold during transit from the airport to the clinic.','疫苗從機場運送到診所的途中一直保持低溫。','in transit / transit from A to B','Noun: the process of moving goods or people from one place to another.','The vaccines are being transported between locations.'),C('transit.s2','公共交通','The city plans to improve public transit for residents outside the centre.','市政府計畫改善市中心以外居民的公共交通。','public transit / transit system','Noun: a local public transport system, or passage through a place.','The plan concerns the network used by passengers.'),C('transit.s3','穿越','The spacecraft will transit the planet’s shadow during the observation.','觀測期間，太空船將穿過行星的陰影。','transit + place or region (verb)','Verb: pass across or through a place.','The spacecraft crosses the shadowed region.')],[M('The parcel was in transit, meaning it had been delivered and would not move again.','The parcel was in transit, meaning it was still being moved to its destination.','In transit means in the process of transportation, not already stationary at the destination.')],[Q('transit.q1','transit.s1','meaning','If vaccines are in transit, what is happening?','They are being moved between locations.','They have been permanently stored at the clinic.','They are being copied into a transcript.','Transit is the process of moving goods or people.'),Q('transit.q2','transit.s2','context','What does a public transit plan improve?','The local network of public transportation.','A patient’s blood transfusion.','A student’s grade transcript.','Public transit means a local transport system.'),Q('transit.q3','transit.s3','distinction','What does it mean for a spacecraft to transit a shadow?','It passes across or through the shadow.','It remains fixed outside the shadow.','It becomes a public bus.','The verb means pass across or through.'),Q('transit.q4','transit.s1','word-choice','Which phrase uses the shipment sense?','the medicine remained cold in transit','take public transit to work','the planet transited the field of view','“In transit” describes goods being moved.')]);
P('transition','From Latin transitionem, “a going across,” from transire “to pass over.”',[C('transition.s1','变化与过渡','The transition from paper files to digital records took several months.','從紙本檔案轉換到數位紀錄花了幾個月。','transition from A to B','Noun: a change from one state, subject, or condition to another.','The workplace changes its record system.'),C('transition.s2','转变过程','The city is transitioning to electric buses over the next five years.','該市將在未來五年逐步轉用電動巴士。','transition to + new system or state','Verb: change from one state or system to another.','The city gradually adopts a new transport system.')],[M('The transition to digital files left the office’s system exactly the same as before.','The transition to digital files changed how the office stores and finds records.','A transition is a change from one state or system to another.')],[Q('transition.q1','transition.s1','meaning','What does a transition from paper files to digital records involve?','A change from one system to another.','A list of spoken words only.','A short film preview.','The noun names a change between states or systems.'),Q('transition.q2','transition.s2','context','If a city is transitioning to electric buses, what is it doing?','Changing its bus system toward electric vehicles.','Keeping the system unchanged.','Transcribing the bus schedule.','The verb describes changing from one system to another.'),Q('transition.q3','transition.s1','distinction','Which phrase is a noun for a period of change?','the transition from school to work','the city transitions to new buses','the train carries a trainload','“The transition” names the change itself.'),Q('transition.q4','transition.s2','grammar','Which sentence uses transition as a verb?','The company is transitioning to a four-day week.','The transition took several months.','We discussed the transition at the meeting.','“Is transitioning” describes the company changing systems.')]);
P('transitional','From transition + -al, meaning relating to or occurring during a change.',[C('transitional.s1','过渡阶段','The transitional housing programme gives families temporary homes while they find permanent ones.','過渡性住房計畫在家庭尋找永久住所期間提供臨時住所。','transitional + period, stage, or service','Adjective: relating to or occurring during a transition.','The housing supports people while they move between living situations.')],[M('The transitional programme offered permanent homes and had no connection to any period of change.','The transitional programme offered temporary homes while families moved toward permanent housing.','Transitional describes support or conditions during a change between states.')],[Q('transitional.q1','transitional.s1','meaning','Why is the housing programme called transitional?','It supports families while they move toward permanent homes.','It guarantees their current situation never changes.','It teaches them to drive a tram.','Transitional means relating to a period of change.'),Q('transitional.q2','transitional.s1','context','What is a transitional stage in a project?','A phase occurring while the project changes to a new arrangement.','The final permanent arrangement only.','A written copy of the project speech.','The adjective describes something occurring during a transition.'),Q('transitional.q3','transitional.s1','distinction','Which service is transitional?','Temporary support while a family moves to permanent housing.','A permanent home with no move or change.','An unrelated film trailer.','Temporary support bridges a change in living situation.'),Q('transitional.q4','transitional.s1','word-choice','Which phrase uses transitional naturally?','a transitional period between two school systems','a transitional fact that never relates to change','a transitional tray carrying cups','The phrase names a period while systems change.')]);
P('transitory','From Latin transitorius, “passing away,” from transire “to pass.”',[C('transitory.s1','短暂存在','The glow of the sunset was transitory and faded within minutes.','夕陽的光輝轉瞬即逝，幾分鐘內便消退了。','transitory + condition or pleasure','Adjective: lasting only a short time before disappearing.','The glow soon disappears.'),C('transitory.s2','稍纵即逝','The critic argued that the celebrity’s fame was transitory and unlikely to last.','評論家認為這位名人的聲望只是曇花一現，不太可能持久。','transitory fame / value','Adjective: passing quickly and leaving little lasting value.','The fame will not have a durable effect.')],[M('The transitory sunset glow remained unchanged for a century.','The transitory sunset glow faded within a few minutes.','Transitory means short-lived or passing, not permanent.')],[Q('transitory.q1','transitory.s1','meaning','What does a transitory glow do?','It lasts briefly and then disappears.','It remains unchanged for centuries.','It carries people across a continent.','The first sense is lasting only briefly.'),Q('transitory.q2','transitory.s2','context','Why might fame be called transitory?','It may pass quickly and leave little lasting value.','It is guaranteed to last forever.','It is a form of public transit.','This sense emphasizes a short-lived quality.'),Q('transitory.q3','transitory.s1','distinction','Which use describes a temporary physical effect?','a transitory flash that vanished','transitory fame among the public','a permanent reputation across generations','The flash is a brief effect.'),Q('transitory.q4','transitory.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses the evaluative sense?','transitory popularity with no lasting influence','a transitory beam lasting only a second','a short transitory delay before a door opens','The first refers to passing fame with little lasting value.')]);
P('translate','From Latin translatus, the past participle of transferre “to carry across”; the language sense developed for carrying meaning across languages.',[C('translate.s1','语言翻译','She translated the safety instructions into Spanish for the visiting workers.','她把安全指示翻譯成西班牙文，供來訪工人閱讀。','translate + text + into + language','Verb: change speech or writing from one language into another.','The instructions are rendered in another language.'),C('translate.s2','转化与结果','The research team translated its findings into a practical guide for farmers.','研究團隊把研究成果轉化成農民可用的實用指南。','translate ideas into action / form','Verb: change something into a different form, or result in something.','Research is turned into a usable guide.'),C('translate.s3','调任','The judge was translated to a different court in the northern district.','那名法官被調任到北部地區的另一所法院。','be translated to + place or post (formal / historical)','Verb: move someone, especially an official or bishop, to another place.','The judge is reassigned to another court.')],[M('She translated the instructions into Spanish by leaving every sentence in English.','She translated the instructions into Spanish by expressing their meaning in Spanish.','Translating into a language requires rendering the message in that language.')],[Q('translate.q1','translate.s1','meaning','What did she do when she translated the instructions into Spanish?','She expressed the English text in Spanish.','She moved the workers to another court.','She changed a geometric shape by rotation.','The language sense changes text from one language to another.'),Q('translate.q2','translate.s2','context','How did the researchers translate findings into a guide?','They turned research into a practical form.','They copied the findings word for word into another language only.','They put the guide on a train.','Translate can mean change one thing into another form.'),Q('translate.q3','translate.s3','distinction','What happened when the judge was translated to a different court?','The judge was reassigned to another place.','The judge’s speech was translated into Spanish.','The court changed its ruling into a chart.','The formal sense means move an official to another post or place.'),Q('translate.q4','translate.s1','word-choice','Which sentence uses the language sense?','The volunteers translated the notice into Mandarin.','The plan translated into lower costs.','The bishop was translated to a new post.','“Into Mandarin” identifies a change of language.')]);
P('translation','From translate + -ion; translate derives through Latin translatus, “carried across.”',[C('translation.s1','语言文本','The translation preserves the humour of the original story.','譯文保留了原故事的幽默感。','a translation of / into + language','Noun: the process of expressing meaning in another language, or the resulting text.','The translated story is a text in another language.'),C('translation.s2','科学与几何','In geometry, a translation shifts a figure without rotating it.','在幾何中，平移會移動圖形但不使其旋轉。','a translation of a figure','Noun: a shift of a figure without rotation, or protein synthesis from RNA.','The figure changes position while keeping its orientation.')],[M('The geometric translation rotated the triangle through ninety degrees without shifting its position.','The geometric translation shifted the triangle without rotating it.','A geometric translation shifts position but does not rotate a figure.')],[Q('translation.q1','translation.s1','meaning','What is a translation of a story?','A version that expresses the story’s meaning in another language.','A figure shifted without rotation.','A list of a student’s grades.','The language sense is a translated text or the process of producing it.'),Q('translation.q2','translation.s2','context','What happens to a figure under geometric translation?','It shifts position without rotating.','It rotates but stays in exactly the same position.','It becomes a written speech transcript.','The geometric sense moves a figure without rotation.'),Q('translation.q3','translation.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses translation for language?','The Chinese translation preserves the joke.','The translation moved the shape to the right.','The cell carried out protein translation.','The Chinese version expresses the story in another language.'),Q('translation.q4','translation.s2','word-choice','Which phrase fits geometry?','a translation of the triangle by five units','a translation of the poem into French','a translation of the interview from audio','The triangle is shifted spatially without being rotated.')]);
P('translucent','From Latin translucere, “to shine through,” formed from trans- + lucere “shine.”',[C('translucent.s1','材料与光线','The lampshade is translucent, so it softens the bulb’s light without hiding it completely.','這個燈罩是半透明的，能柔化燈泡的光，卻不會完全遮住光線。','translucent + material or surface','Adjective: allowing some light through but not fully clear.','Light passes through, while objects are not sharply visible.'),C('translucent.s2','文风清晰','Her translucent prose makes a complicated scientific idea easy to follow.','她清晰明白的文筆讓複雜的科學概念容易理解。','translucent prose / explanation (figurative)','Adjective: clear and easy to understand.','The explanation is not obscure.')],[M('The translucent glass blocked every ray of light and made the room completely dark.','The translucent glass let some light into the room while blurring the view.','Translucent material allows some light through; opaque material blocks it.')],[Q('translucent.q1','translucent.s1','meaning','How does a translucent lampshade affect light?','It lets some light pass through but blurs the view.','It blocks every ray of light.','It lets a perfectly sharp image through.','Translucent is not fully clear but does allow some light through.'),Q('translucent.q2','translucent.s2','context','Why call the prose translucent?','Its ideas are clear and easy to understand.','Its pages let sunlight pass through.','It hides every point from readers.','The figurative sense means clear in expression.'),Q('translucent.q3','translucent.s1','distinction','Which material is translucent?','A panel that glows with light but blurs objects behind it.','A black panel that admits no light.','A clear window showing sharp details.','The panel passes light without being fully transparent.'),Q('translucent.q4','translucent.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses the figurative sense?','a translucent explanation of the theory','a translucent curtain that softens daylight','a translucent plastic sheet letting light through','An explanation can be translucent when it is easy to follow.')]);
P('transmigration','From Latin transmigratio, from trans- “across” + migrare “to move.”',[C('transmigration.s1','人口迁移','The government’s transmigration programme moved families from crowded islands to new settlements.','政府的遷居計畫把家庭從人口密集的島嶼遷往新聚落。','transmigration of people between regions','Noun: movement of people from one country or region to settle in another.','Families relocate to a new region.'),C('transmigration.s2','宗教观念','The doctrine describes the transmigration of a soul into another body after death.','這種教義描述靈魂死後轉入另一個身體。','transmigration of the soul','Noun: the passage of a soul into another body after death.','The soul is believed to continue in a different body.')],[M('The doctrine’s transmigration of the soul meant it remained in the same body forever.','The doctrine’s transmigration of the soul meant it passed into another body after death.','The religious sense is passage of a soul into another body, not remaining in the same one.')],[Q('transmigration.q1','transmigration.s1','meaning','What did the government’s transmigration programme do?','Moved people to settle in a different region.','Moved a soul into another body after death.','Changed a written text into another language.','The first sense concerns people relocating between regions.'),Q('transmigration.q2','transmigration.s2','context','What happens in the doctrine of transmigration of the soul?','The soul passes into another body after death.','The soul remains in the same body forever.','A family settles in a new island region.','This religious sense describes the soul’s passage to another body.'),Q('transmigration.q3','transmigration.s1','distinction','Which example concerns human migration?','Families move from a crowded island to a new settlement.','A soul is believed to enter another body.','A cell copies DNA into RNA.','Relocating families is the population sense.'),Q('transmigration.q4','transmigration.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses the religious sense?','belief in the transmigration of souls','a government plan for rural transmigration','a transmigration programme moving households','“Souls” identifies the belief about passage after death.')]);
P('transmission','From Latin transmissio, from transmittere “to send across.”',[C('transmission.s1','传播','The rapid transmission of the virus was reduced by better ventilation.','改善通風後，病毒的快速傳播有所減少。','transmission of + signal, message, disease, or quality','Noun: the act of passing a signal, message, or disease between people or places.','The virus passes from one person or place to another.'),C('transmission.s2','广播信号','The radio transmission reached ships far beyond the coastline.','無線電傳輸訊號傳到了遠離海岸的船隻。','radio / television transmission','Noun: broadcasting a radio or television signal.','The signal is sent out to distant receivers.'),C('transmission.s3','汽车部件','The mechanic repaired the transmission that carries engine power to the wheels.','技師修好了把引擎動力傳到車輪的變速傳動裝置。','a manual / automatic transmission','Noun: the vehicle part that carries power from the engine to the wheels.','This component transfers engine power to the wheels.')],[M('The car’s transmission carried the radio broadcast from the antenna to distant ships.','The radio transmitter sent the broadcast to distant ships; the car’s transmission carried engine power to its wheels.','Transmission may mean a broadcast or a vehicle power-transfer part; the latter does not carry radio signals.')],[Q('transmission.q1','transmission.s1','meaning','What does transmission of a virus mean?','The virus passes between people or places.','A car sends engine power to its wheels.','A student changes schools.','This sense is the passing of a disease from one person or place to another.'),Q('transmission.q2','transmission.s2','context','What reached distant ships in a radio transmission?','A broadcast signal.','A car’s engine power.','An official transcript.','Radio transmission is broadcasting a signal.'),Q('transmission.q3','transmission.s3','distinction','What did the mechanic repair in the car?','The part that carries engine power to the wheels.','The radio broadcast sent to the ships.','The spread of a virus.','The automotive transmission carries power from engine to wheels.'),Q('transmission.q4','transmission.s1','word-choice','Which phrase refers to disease spread?','transmission of the infection between households','transmission of radio news across the sea','the car’s transmission failed','The infection moves between households.')]);
P('transmit','From Latin transmittere, “to send across,” from trans- + mittere “send.”',[C('transmit.s1','电子通信','The station transmits emergency updates every fifteen minutes.','電台每十五分鐘播送一次緊急更新。','transmit a signal / message / programme','Verb: send an electronic signal, message, or programme.','The station broadcasts information to receivers.'),C('transmit.s2','疾病与特征','Some mosquitoes transmit the virus when they bite an infected host.','有些蚊子叮咬受感染宿主時會傳播病毒。','transmit a disease / heat / quality','Verb: pass a disease, heat, or quality from one person or thing to another.','The mosquito carries the virus between hosts.')],[M('The radio station transmitted emergency updates by keeping the signal switched off.','The radio station transmitted emergency updates by broadcasting them to listeners.','Transmit a programme or signal means send it electronically, not switch it off.')],[Q('transmit.q1','transmit.s1','meaning','What does a station do when it transmits updates?','It sends or broadcasts them electronically.','It stores them without sending them.','It transfers the presenters to another school.','The communications sense is sending a signal or programme.'),Q('transmit.q2','transmit.s2','context','How can a mosquito transmit a virus?','It can pass the virus between hosts when it bites.','It broadcasts the virus as a radio programme.','It writes down the virus word for word.','The biological sense means pass a disease from one host to another.'),Q('transmit.q3','transmit.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses transmit for a broadcast?','The station transmitted the warning over the radio.','The mosquito transmitted the infection to a host.','Heat transmitted through the metal rod.','The radio warning is an electronic signal.'),Q('transmit.q4','transmit.s2','word-choice','Which phrase describes disease spread?','transmit malaria from one host to another','transmit a television programme at noon','transmit a message by radio','Malaria is passed between hosts.')]);
P('transmitter','From transmit + -er, a device or living source that sends or passes something on.',[C('transmitter.s1','无线电设备','The technicians replaced the transmitter on the hill to restore the radio signal.','技術人員更換了山上的發射器，以恢復無線電訊號。','a radio / television transmitter','Noun: a device that sends out radio or television signals.','The equipment emits the broadcast signal.'),C('transmitter.s2','疾病传播者','Researchers identified the mosquito as a transmitter of the parasite.','研究人員確認蚊子是這種寄生蟲的傳播者。','a transmitter of + disease or message','Noun: a person or animal that passes something to others.','The mosquito carries the parasite to another host.')],[M('The transmitter on the hill received no signal and was not able to send one out.','The transmitter on the hill sent the radio signal to receivers across the valley.','A transmitter sends out a signal; a receiver takes one in.')],[Q('transmitter.q1','transmitter.s1','meaning','What does a radio transmitter do?','Sends out a signal for receivers to pick up.','Receives every signal but sends none.','Carries engine power to car wheels.','The device sense is equipment that emits radio or television signals.'),Q('transmitter.q2','transmitter.s2','context','Why is a mosquito called a transmitter of a parasite?','It can pass the parasite to another host.','It broadcasts a radio signal.','It copies a student’s grades.','The biological sense is a carrier that passes something to others.'),Q('transmitter.q3','transmitter.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses transmitter for a device?','The hilltop transmitter sent the station’s signal.','The mosquito was a transmitter of the disease.','The infected animal transmitted the parasite.','The hilltop equipment sends out a signal.'),Q('transmitter.q4','transmitter.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses the carrier sense?','an animal transmitter of the infection','a transmitter broadcasting a television signal','a transmitter mounted on the radio tower','The animal passes an infection to other hosts.')]);
P('transmute','From Latin transmutare, “to change across or alter,” from trans- + mutare.',[C('transmute.s1','艺术转化','The poet transmuted grief into a sequence of vivid images.','詩人把悲傷轉化成一連串鮮明的意象。','transmute A into B','Verb: change something completely in form or nature.','The emotion becomes a different kind of expression.'),C('transmute.s2','自然变化','Under intense pressure, the mineral can transmute into a denser crystal form.','在強大壓力下，這種礦物可以轉變成更緻密的晶體形態。','transmute into + new form','Verb: change in form or quality by itself.','The mineral changes into another form under pressure.')],[M('The poet transmuted grief into a poem by leaving the grief completely unchanged and producing no poem.','The poet transmuted grief into a poem by reshaping the emotion as language and images.','To transmute A into B is to change A into a different form.')],[Q('transmute.q1','transmute.s1','meaning','What did the poet do by transmuting grief into images?','Changed the emotion into a different expressive form.','Kept it unchanged and wrote nothing.','Sent it as a radio signal.','The verb means change something completely in form or nature.'),Q('transmute.q2','transmute.s2','context','What happened to the mineral under pressure?','It changed into a denser crystal form.','It remained exactly the same.','It became a written transcript.','The second sense describes something changing form by itself.'),Q('transmute.q3','transmute.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses transmute with an object?','The artist transmuted fear into music.','The mineral transmuted under heat.','The crystal transmuted into another form.','The artist acts on fear and changes it into music.'),Q('transmute.q4','transmute.s2','word-choice','Which phrase describes a material changing form?','the metal transmuted into a new substance','the composer transmuted sorrow into a song','the writer transmuted a speech into a transcript','The first phrase presents material change rather than artistic transformation.')]);
P('transparency','From transparent + -cy, naming the quality of being see-through or open to scrutiny.',[C('transparency.s1','光学','The transparency of the thin glass made the bird feeder easy to inspect.','薄玻璃的透明度讓人容易查看餵鳥器內部。','transparency of + material','Noun: the quality of allowing light through so objects can be seen.','The glass lets the viewer see through it.'),C('transparency.s2','公开与诚信','The committee published its minutes to improve transparency in decision-making.','委員會公布會議紀錄，以提高決策過程的透明度。','transparency in + process or institution','Noun: openness and honesty that let others see how things work.' ,'Publishing minutes makes the process easier to scrutinize.'),C('transparency.s3','投影胶片','The lecturer placed a transparency on the overhead projector.','講師把一張投影片放到高架投影機上。','a transparency (projected sheet)','Noun: a clear plastic sheet with an image for projection.','The sheet carries an image to project.')],[M('The committee hid every decision and record to increase transparency in its work.','The committee published its records to increase transparency in its work.','Transparency in governance means openness, not hiding decisions.')],[Q('transparency.q1','transparency.s1','meaning','What does the transparency of glass describe?','How well light passes through so objects can be seen.','How openly a committee publishes decisions.','How many trainloads the glass can carry.','The material sense is the quality of being see-through.'),Q('transparency.q2','transparency.s2','context','Why publish meeting minutes to improve transparency?','It lets the public see how decisions are made.','It makes the glass more transparent.','It turns the minutes into a projected plastic sheet.','Institutional transparency means openness about processes.'),Q('transparency.q3','transparency.s3','distinction','What did the lecturer place on the projector?','A clear plastic sheet carrying an image.','A committee’s public records.','A pane of glass used in a feeder.','A transparency can be a sheet for projection.'),Q('transparency.q4','transparency.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses the openness sense?','transparency in public spending','transparency of the glass pane','a transparency projected in class','Public spending transparency lets people scrutinize decisions.')]);
P('transparent','From Medieval Latin transparens, “shining through,” from trans- + parere “appear.”',[C('transparent.s1','材料透光','The transparent lid lets visitors see the specimen without opening the case.','透明的蓋子讓訪客不用打開展櫃也能看見標本。','transparent + glass, plastic, or material','Adjective: allowing light through so objects behind can be seen.','The specimen remains visible through the lid.'),C('transparent.s2','容易看懂','The manual uses transparent language to explain the complicated controls.','手冊用清楚易懂的語言解釋複雜的控制裝置。','transparent explanation / argument','Adjective: easy to understand or to see the truth of.','The wording makes the information clear.'),C('transparent.s3','公开决策','The agency promised a transparent process for awarding the contracts.','該機構承諾以公開透明的程序頒發合約。','a transparent process / government','Adjective: open so people can see how decisions are made.','The agency allows the decision process to be scrutinized.')],[M('The agency called its secret, unreviewable contract process transparent.','The agency made its contract process transparent by publishing the criteria and decisions.','A transparent process is open to scrutiny, not secret.')],[Q('transparent.q1','transparent.s1','meaning','Why is the display lid transparent?','Visitors can see the specimen through it.','It blocks all light and hides the specimen.','It explains the controls in simple words.','The material sense allows light through so objects can be seen.'),Q('transparent.q2','transparent.s2','context','What is transparent language in a manual?','Language that is clear and easy to understand.','Language hidden from every reader.','Language printed on a clear sheet only.','This figurative sense means easy to understand.'),Q('transparent.q3','transparent.s3','distinction','What makes a contract process transparent?','People can see the criteria and how decisions are made.','No one can inspect the decision process.','The paperwork is physically made of glass.','The process sense is open to public scrutiny.'),Q('transparent.q4','transparent.s1','word-choice','Which use is literal?','a transparent pane showing the plant behind it','a transparent excuse that everyone sees through','a transparent bidding process','The pane physically lets light through.')]);
P('transpiration','From Latin transpirationem, from transpirare “to breathe through.”',[C('transpiration.s1','植物生理','On a hot afternoon, transpiration carries water vapour from the leaves through tiny stomata.','炎熱的午後，蒸散作用會使水蒸氣經由葉片上的微小氣孔散出。','transpiration from leaves through stomata','Noun: loss of water vapour from a plant, mainly through leaf stomata.','Water leaves the plant as vapour through small openings.')],[M('The botanist said transpiration meant water vapour entering leaves from the air and remaining there.','The botanist said transpiration is water vapour leaving a plant, mainly through leaf stomata.','Plant transpiration is water loss as vapour, not vapour entering and remaining.')],[Q('transpiration.q1','transpiration.s1','meaning','What leaves a plant during transpiration?','Water vapour, mainly through leaf stomata.','A radio signal from the roots.','Blood entering the plant’s circulation.','The botanical sense is loss of water vapour from a plant.'),Q('transpiration.q2','transpiration.s1','context','Where does most leaf transpiration occur?','Through tiny openings called stomata.','Through the wooden stem’s bark only.','Through a transparent glass cover.','Stomata are the principal openings for water-vapour loss.'),Q('transpiration.q3','transpiration.s1','distinction','Which observation concerns transpiration?','A plant loses water vapour through its leaves.','A person receives blood through an IV line.','A signal travels from a radio tower.','The first observation describes plant water loss.'),Q('transpiration.q4','transpiration.s1','word-choice','Which phrase is botanically accurate?','transpiration draws water up as vapour leaves the foliage','transpiration is the copying of DNA into RNA','transpiration is a type of public transportation','The plant loses water vapour through its foliage.')]);
P('transpire','From Latin transpirare, “to breathe through,” from trans- + spirare “breathe.”',[C('transpire.s1','事情发生','A scheduling problem transpired during the final stage of the project.','專案最後階段發生了排程問題。','it transpired that + event (formal)','Verb: happen, especially in a way not previously known.','The problem occurred during the project.'),C('transpire.s2','后来得知','It later transpired that the missing files had been archived rather than deleted.','後來才得知，遺失的檔案其實被封存，而非刪除。','it transpired that + fact','Verb: become known over time.','The fact was revealed later.')],[M('It later transpired that the files were missing, but this had been publicly known from the beginning.','It later transpired that the files were missing, a fact no one had known before.','In this use, transpire means become known later; “later” conflicts with already being known from the start.')],[Q('transpire.q1','transpire.s1','meaning','What transpired during the project’s final stage?','A scheduling problem happened.','A hidden fact became known later only.','The project crossed a continent.','The first sense is to happen or occur.'),Q('transpire.q2','transpire.s2','context','What does “It later transpired that the files were archived” mean?','People later learned that the files had been archived.','The files physically breathed through the archive.','The files were translated into another language.','The second sense means become known over time.'),Q('transpire.q3','transpire.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses transpire for an event occurring?','A delay transpired while the team changed systems.','It transpired that the delay had been concealed.','The truth transpired years after the trial.','The first sentence reports something that happened.'),Q('transpire.q4','transpire.s2','word-choice','Which phrase signals the “become known” sense?','It eventually transpired that the report was incomplete.','The meeting transpired at noon.','A leaf transpires water vapour.','“Eventually it transpired that” introduces a fact revealed later.')]);
P('transplant','From trans- “across” + plant; medical use extends the idea of moving living tissue to another place.',[C('transplant.s1','医疗与园艺','Surgeons transplanted a healthy kidney from the donor to the recipient.','外科醫生把健康的腎臟從捐贈者移植到受贈者體內。','transplant an organ / plant to + place','Verb: move an organ, tissue, or plant to another body or place.','The kidney is moved into another person.'),C('transplant.s2','移植手术','The patient recovered well after a liver transplant.','肝臟移植手術後，病人恢復良好。','a kidney / liver / heart transplant','Noun: an operation moving an organ, or the organ moved.','The phrase names the surgical operation.')],[M('The surgeons called it a transplant, but they left the donor kidney in its original body and performed no operation.','The surgeons performed a transplant by moving the donor kidney into the recipient.','A transplant is the operation or organ moved to another body.')],[Q('transplant.q1','transplant.s1','meaning','What did the surgeons do when they transplanted the kidney?','Moved it from the donor into the recipient.','Left it in the donor and did nothing.','Copied its medical record into a transcript.','The verb means move an organ or tissue to another body.'),Q('transplant.q2','transplant.s2','context','What does “a liver transplant” name?','An operation that moves a liver, or the organ moved.','A blood test that measures current flow.','A journey across a continent.','The noun can refer to the operation or the organ.'),Q('transplant.q3','transplant.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses transplant as a verb?','The surgeon transplanted the tissue into the patient.','She recovered after a transplant.','The transplant donor was thanked.','“Transplanted” describes the action of moving tissue.'),Q('transplant.q4','transplant.s2','word-choice','Which phrase is the medical noun?','She is waiting for a kidney transplant.','They transplant flowers in spring.','The clinic transplanted the organ yesterday.','The noun names the operation or organ.')]);
P('transplantation','From transplant + -ation, naming the transfer of an organ, tissue, or living plant.',[C('transplantation.s1','器官移植','Advances in kidney transplantation have made the operation safer for many patients.','腎臟移植技術的進步讓許多病人的手術更加安全。','organ / tissue transplantation','Noun: surgical transfer of an organ or tissue from a donor, or replanting a living plant.','The medical process moves tissue from a donor to a recipient.')],[M('The team described transplantation as leaving the donor organ untouched and never placing it in a recipient.','The team described transplantation as moving an organ from a donor into a recipient.','Transplantation involves transferring an organ or tissue, not leaving it in place.')],[Q('transplantation.q1','transplantation.s1','meaning','What is kidney transplantation?','The surgical transfer of a kidney to a recipient.','A written copy of a kidney’s medical record.','A method of measuring radio transmission.','The medical sense is surgical transfer of an organ or tissue.'),Q('transplantation.q2','transplantation.s1','context','What does transplantation mean for a garden plant?','Moving and replanting the living plant elsewhere.','Sending its signal by radio.','Changing it into a written transcript.','The same word can describe replanting a living plant.'),Q('transplantation.q3','transplantation.s1','distinction','Which procedure is transplantation?','Moving donor tissue into a recipient’s body.','Taking a blood sample for testing.','Changing a patient’s hospital room.','The donor tissue is surgically transferred.'),Q('transplantation.q4','transplantation.s1','word-choice','Which phrase is natural?','advances in liver transplantation','transplantation of a radio programme to listeners','transplantation of a student’s transcript','The first phrase names a medical organ-transfer procedure.')]);
P('transport','From Latin transportare, “to carry across,” from trans- + portare “carry.”',[C('transport.s1','货物与人员','The ferry transports residents and supplies between the island and the mainland.','渡輪在島嶼與大陸之間運送居民和補給品。','transport people / goods from A to B','Verb: take goods or people from one place to another.','Passengers and supplies are moved between places.'),C('transport.s2','交通方式','Public transport is cheaper than driving into the city centre.','搭乘公共交通比開車進入市中心便宜。','by public transport','Noun: a system for carrying people or goods.','The phrase refers to the network of buses, trains, and similar services.')],[M('The ferry transported supplies by keeping them on the island instead of taking them anywhere.','The ferry transported supplies from the island to the mainland.','To transport something is to take it from one place to another.')],[Q('transport.q1','transport.s1','meaning','What does the ferry transport?','It carries residents and supplies between places.','It leaves all passengers in the same place.','It records the passengers’ grades.','The verb means take people or goods to another place.'),Q('transport.q2','transport.s2','context','What is public transport?','A system such as buses or trains that carries people.','A single person walking a trail.','A written translation of a bus timetable.','The noun sense is a transportation system.'),Q('transport.q3','transport.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses transport as a verb?','The lorry transports food to the village.','Public transport serves the village.','The transport system runs late.','The lorry actively carries food to another place.'),Q('transport.q4','transport.s2','word-choice','Which phrase refers to a system?','The town improved public transport.','The driver transported the boxes.','The boxes were transported yesterday.','Public transport names a system for carrying passengers or goods.')]);
P('transportation','From transport + -ation, naming the act or system of carrying people or goods.',[C('transportation.s1','运输行为','The transportation of fresh fruit by rail reduced delivery costs.','以鐵路運送新鮮水果降低了配送成本。','transportation of + goods or people','Noun: the act of moving people or goods from one place to another.','The fruit is moved between locations.'),C('transportation.s2','交通系统','The city expanded its public transportation with two new bus routes.','該市新增兩條公車路線，擴大公共交通系統。','public transportation','Noun: a system of vehicles and routes used for travel.','The new routes add to the city’s transport network.')],[M('The transportation of the fruit was completed by leaving it in the orchard.','The transportation of the fruit was completed by carrying it to the market.','Transportation means moving people or goods from one place to another.')],[Q('transportation.q1','transportation.s1','meaning','What does transportation of fruit describe?','Moving the fruit from one place to another.','Leaving the fruit where it grew.','Converting the fruit into a transcript.','The first sense names the act of moving goods.'),Q('transportation.q2','transportation.s2','context','What did two new bus routes expand?','The city’s public transportation system.','The number of trainloads at one port.','The transparency of the bus windows.','The system sense includes vehicles and travel routes.'),Q('transportation.q3','transportation.s1','distinction','Which phrase refers to the act of carrying goods?','transportation of grain by rail','the city’s public transportation network','a bus route map','The first phrase names a movement of goods.'),Q('transportation.q4','transportation.s2','word-choice','Which phrase means a travel network?','the region’s transportation system','transportation of furniture to a new home','transporting a patient to hospital','The system, rather than one act, is the network of routes and vehicles.')]);
P('transporter','From transport + -er, naming a vehicle or vessel designed to carry goods.',[C('transporter.s1','货运车辆','The transporter delivered the oversized machine to the construction site.','運輸車把大型機器送到了施工現場。','a transporter for + cargo','Noun: a large vehicle or ship built to carry goods.','The vehicle is built to carry a heavy load.')],[M('The transporter was a tiny passenger bicycle that could carry no cargo.','The transporter was a large vehicle built to carry the machine.','A transporter is a large vehicle or ship for carrying goods.')],[Q('transporter.q1','transporter.s1','meaning','What is a transporter in freight use?','A large vehicle or ship built to carry goods.','A person learning a new skill.','A small film preview.','The noun refers to a cargo-carrying vehicle or vessel.'),Q('transporter.q2','transporter.s1','context','Why did the site hire a transporter for an oversized machine?','It was built to carry large cargo.','It could translate the machine’s manual.','It was a city tram for commuters.','A transporter carries goods, including large equipment.'),Q('transporter.q3','transporter.s1','distinction','Which item is a transporter?','A heavy lorry designed to carry construction machinery.','A person who trains the construction crew.','A ticket for public transit.','The lorry is a large goods-carrying vehicle.'),Q('transporter.q4','transporter.s1','word-choice','Which phrase is natural?','a ship transporter carrying equipment','a transporter teaching the crew to read','a transporter meaning one small hand tool','The ship is designed to transport cargo.')]);
P('transpose','From Latin transponere, “to put across or move,” from trans- + ponere “put.”',[C('transpose.s1','顺序调换','The editor accidentally transposed the two columns, putting dates under the wrong heading.','編輯不慎把兩欄對調，讓日期落在錯誤的標題之下。','transpose A and B / transpose columns','Verb: change the position or order of two or more things.','The columns exchange positions.'),C('transpose.s2','音乐移调','The pianist transposed the song into a lower key for the singer.','鋼琴家把歌曲移調到較低的調性，方便歌手演唱。','transpose music into + key','Verb: move a piece of music into a different key.','The melody is rewritten at a lower pitch level.')],[M('The editor transposed the columns by leaving each one exactly where it was.','The editor transposed the columns by exchanging their positions.','To transpose columns is to change their order or positions.')],[Q('transpose.q1','transpose.s1','meaning','What did the editor do by transposing two columns?','Changed their positions or order.','Translated the headings into another language.','Removed both columns without changing anything.','The general verb means change the position or order.'),Q('transpose.q2','transpose.s2','context','Why did the pianist transpose the song?','To move it into a lower key for the singer.','To change the singer’s school.','To record the song’s lyrics as a transcript.','The music sense means move a composition into another key.'),Q('transpose.q3','transpose.s1','distinction','Which is a positional transposition?','Swapping the names in the first and second columns.','Rewriting a melody in a lower key.','Translating an interview into French.','The columns exchange their order.'),Q('transpose.q4','transpose.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses the musical sense?','transpose the melody into E minor','transpose the table headings','transpose the two rows in the report','E minor is a musical key.')]);
P('transposon','A biological term formed from transpose with the scientific ending -on, naming a DNA element that can change position.',[C('transposon.s1','遗传学','The researchers found a transposon inserted inside a gene that affects flower colour.','研究人員在一個影響花色的基因內發現了一段轉座子。','a transposon inserted into DNA','Noun: a mobile genetic element that can insert itself at another site in DNA.','The DNA element has moved to a new position in the genome.')],[M('The study called a fixed protein molecule a transposon even though it could not move or insert into DNA.','The study identified a mobile DNA element that could insert itself at another site as a transposon.','A transposon is a mobile genetic element that can change its position in DNA.')],[Q('transposon.q1','transposon.s1','meaning','What makes a DNA element a transposon?','It can move and insert at another site in DNA.','It is a fixed protein that never changes location.','It is a radio signal carried across a city.','The defining sense is a mobile genetic element.'),Q('transposon.q2','transposon.s1','context','Where did researchers find the transposon?','Inserted inside a gene affecting flower colour.','Inside a railway carriage.','In a transcript of the research paper only.','A transposon inserts into DNA, including within a gene.'),Q('transposon.q3','transposon.s1','distinction','Which observation supports identifying a transposon?','A DNA segment moves to a new site in the genome.','A protein stays fixed outside the DNA.','An RNA molecule is translated into a poem.','Movement to another DNA site is characteristic of the element.'),Q('transposon.q4','transposon.s1','word-choice','Which phrase is biologically accurate?','a transposon inserted into a new DNA site','a transposon carrying passengers to a station','a transposon as a city tram system','The element can insert itself at another DNA site.')]);
P('trap','From Old English træppe, a device for catching; related forms occur in early Germanic languages.',[C('trap.s1','捕捉装置','The ranger checked the humane trap and released the fox unharmed.','護林員檢查了人道捕捉器，並讓狐狸毫髮無傷地離開。','set / check a trap','Noun: a device or trick for catching an animal or person.' ,'The device is designed to catch an animal.'),C('trap.s2','困住','The hikers were trapped by rising water on the narrow path.','水位上升後，健行者被困在狹窄小徑上。','be trapped in / by + place or danger','Verb: catch something or keep someone in a difficult place.','The hikers cannot leave the flooded path.')],[M('The ranger checked the trap, which had been designed to keep every animal free and uncaught.','The ranger checked the trap to see whether it had caught an animal.','A trap is designed to catch or hold something, not guarantee it remains uncaught.')],[Q('trap.q1','trap.s1','meaning','What is a humane trap used for?','Catching an animal so it can be checked or released.','Keeping every animal away without catching one.','Carrying a load behind a car.','The device sense is something used to catch an animal or person.'),Q('trap.q2','trap.s2','context','Why were hikers trapped by rising water?','They could not leave the flooded path safely.','They had caught a fox in a cage.','They were changing trains at a station.','To trap someone is to keep them in a difficult place.'),Q('trap.q3','trap.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses trap as a noun?','The ranger set a trap near the burrow.','The rising tide trapped the hikers.','The hikers were trapped on the path.','The first sentence names the catching device.'),Q('trap.q4','trap.s2','word-choice','Which sentence uses trap as a verb?','Smoke trapped the campers inside the cabin.','The campers set a trap for the fox.','A trap sat beside the trail.','Smoke keeps the campers from leaving.')]);
P('trapdoor','A compound of trap + door, a concealed or flush-fitting door opened by lifting.',[C('trapdoor.s1','建筑结构','The actor escaped through a trapdoor set flush into the stage floor.','演員從與舞台地面齊平的暗門逃了出去。','through / beneath a trapdoor','Noun: a small door in a floor, wall, or ceiling that opens by lifting.','The panel lies level with the floor and can be lifted.')],[M('The carpenter called a hinged wall standing upright in the corridor a trapdoor in the floor.','The carpenter installed a small lifting door flush with the floor as a trapdoor.','A trapdoor lies in a surface such as a floor and opens by lifting.')],[Q('trapdoor.q1','trapdoor.s1','meaning','Where might a stage trapdoor be found?','Flush with the floor and opened by lifting.','Hanging as a large front entrance gate.','Mounted on a train as a signal.','A trapdoor is a small lifting door in a floor, wall, or ceiling.'),Q('trapdoor.q2','trapdoor.s1','context','How did the actor disappear?','Through a concealed panel in the stage floor.','By climbing onto a trailer.','By changing a melody into a new key.','The trapdoor provides a hidden opening beneath the stage.'),Q('trapdoor.q3','trapdoor.s1','distinction','Which object is a trapdoor?','A small flush panel that lifts from the ceiling.','A broad door that swings at the front of a house.','A movable ladder leaning against a wall.','A small lifting panel in a surface matches the definition.'),Q('trapdoor.q4','trapdoor.s1','word-choice','Which phrase is natural?','open the trapdoor beneath the stage','transmit a trapdoor over the radio','transpose the trapdoor into a key','A trapdoor can be opened to pass through a floor or ceiling.')]);
P('trapeze','From French trapèze, ultimately Greek trapezion, “little table.”',[C('trapeze.s1','杂技表演','The acrobat swung from the trapeze and caught her partner’s hands.','雜技演員從高空鞦韆盪出，抓住了搭檔的雙手。','swing / perform on a trapeze','Noun: a horizontal bar suspended by ropes for an acrobat to swing on.','The bar hangs from ropes above the performance space.')],[M('The acrobat performed on a trapeze, a horizontal bar resting firmly on the floor with no ropes.','The acrobat performed on a trapeze, a horizontal bar suspended by ropes.','A trapeze is suspended by ropes so an acrobat can swing on it.')],[Q('trapeze.q1','trapeze.s1','meaning','What is a trapeze?','A horizontal bar hanging from ropes for an acrobat.','A four-sided shape with parallel sides.','A floor panel opened by lifting.','The circus apparatus is a suspended bar.'),Q('trapeze.q2','trapeze.s1','context','What did the acrobat do from the trapeze?','Swung and caught her partner’s hands.','Carried a shipment across a continent.','Transcribed the music for brass.','The bar is used for swinging acrobatic performance.'),Q('trapeze.q3','trapeze.s1','distinction','Which item belongs in a circus act?','A rope-suspended horizontal bar.','A geometric quadrilateral.','A freight vehicle.','The suspended bar is a trapeze.'),Q('trapeze.q4','trapeze.s1','word-choice','Which phrase uses trapeze correctly?','the acrobat swung high above the net on the trapeze','the trapeze listed the student’s grades','the trapeze moved the city bus underground','The phrase describes an acrobat using the apparatus.')]);
P('trapezoid','From Greek trapezoeides, “table-shaped,” from trapeza “table” + -oeides “like.”',[C('trapezoid.s1','几何','In American usage, the worksheet defines a trapezoid as a quadrilateral with exactly one pair of parallel sides.','在美式用法中，練習單把梯形定義為恰有一組平行邊的四邊形。','a trapezoid with + geometric property','Noun: in American English, a quadrilateral with exactly one pair of parallel sides; British usage often differs.','The definition follows the stated American convention.')],[M('The worksheet called a circle a trapezoid even though it had no four sides.','The worksheet called the four-sided figure with one pair of parallel sides a trapezoid.','A trapezoid is a quadrilateral; a circle has no sides.')],[Q('trapezoid.q1','trapezoid.s1','meaning','Under the worksheet’s American definition, what is a trapezoid?','A four-sided shape with exactly one pair of parallel sides.','A circle with no sides.','A suspended acrobat’s bar.','The stated American sense is a quadrilateral with one parallel pair.'),Q('trapezoid.q2','trapezoid.s1','context','Why should an international geometry class note regional usage of trapezoid?','British English often uses a different definition.','The word means a rail vehicle everywhere.','The word is used only for a theatre door.','The source explicitly notes a British-American difference.'),Q('trapezoid.q3','trapezoid.s1','distinction','Which shape fits the American sense given here?','A quadrilateral with one pair of parallel sides.','A triangle with three parallel sides.','A circle with no straight edges.','The first is the defined four-sided figure.'),Q('trapezoid.q4','trapezoid.s1','word-choice','Which statement is careful and accurate?','In American usage, the trapezoid has exactly one parallel pair.','Every English variety uses trapezoid with an identical definition.','A trapezoid is a rope-suspended circus bar.','The source warns that British usage often differs.')]);
P('trapper','From trap + -er, meaning a person who catches animals in traps.',[C('trapper.s1','野外生活','The trapper checked his line at dawn and recorded which animals had passed.','捕獸者黎明時查看陷阱線，並記錄有哪些動物經過。','a trapper of + animals','Noun: someone who catches animals, especially fur-bearing mammals, in traps.','The person sets and checks traps for animals.')],[M('The trapper spent the morning training foxes but set no traps or caught any animals.','The trapper spent the morning checking traps set for wild animals.','A trapper is someone who catches animals using traps.')],[Q('trapper.q1','trapper.s1','meaning','What does a trapper do?','Catches animals, often fur-bearing mammals, with traps.','Trains a team to use computers.','Translates a novel into French.','The noun describes someone who catches animals in traps.'),Q('trapper.q2','trapper.s1','context','Why did the trapper check his line at dawn?','To see whether animals had been caught.','To send a radio broadcast.','To change a song into another key.','Checking traps is part of the trapper’s work.'),Q('trapper.q3','trapper.s1','distinction','Which person is a trapper?','Someone who sets traps to catch wild mammals.','Someone who studies the shape of a trapezoid.','Someone who carries cargo by ship.','The first person catches animals in traps.'),Q('trapper.q4','trapper.s1','word-choice','Which phrase is natural?','a trapper checked the animal traps','a trapper checked the film trailer','a trapper transcribed the rail route','The phrase matches the animal-catching occupation.')]);
P('trash','Origin uncertain; recorded in Middle English for discarded or worthless material, later also used as a verb.',[C('trash.s1','废弃物','Please put the empty cartons in the trash before leaving the studio.','離開工作室前，請把空紙盒放進垃圾桶。','put / take out the trash','Noun: things thrown away, or something of very poor quality.','The cartons are waste to be discarded.'),C('trash.s2','毁坏与抨击','The angry crowd trashed the empty office after the match.','比賽後，憤怒的人群破壞了空置的辦公室。','trash a place / trash a film (informal)','Verb: damage a place badly, or criticize someone or something harshly.','The crowd badly damages the office.')],[M('The crowd trashed the office by carefully repairing every broken window and leaving it better than before.','The crowd trashed the office by smashing windows and damaging the furniture.','To trash a place is to damage it badly, not repair it.')],[Q('trash.q1','trash.s1','meaning','What belongs in the trash?','Items that are being thrown away.','An official record of university grades.','A rope-suspended circus bar.','The noun means discarded material or something of very poor quality.'),Q('trash.q2','trash.s2','context','What did the crowd do when it trashed the office?','Damaged the place badly.','Cleaned and repaired every room.','Carried the furniture to another building carefully.','The verb sense means cause serious damage.'),Q('trash.q3','trash.s2','distinction','Which sentence uses trash to mean criticize harshly?','The reviewer trashed the sequel in a scathing article.','The crew took the trash outside.','The crowd trashed the empty office.','A reviewer can trash a film by criticizing it harshly.'),Q('trash.q4','trash.s1','word-choice','Which phrase uses trash as waste?','put the empty cartons in the trash','trash the hotel room','trash the film in a review','The cartons are discarded rubbish.')]);
P('trash can','A compound of trash + can, the common North American term for a rubbish container.',[C('trash can.s1','家居用品','She dropped the folded paper into the trash can beside the desk.','她把摺好的紙丟進書桌旁的垃圾桶。','put something in / empty a trash can','Noun: a container that holds rubbish until it is emptied.','The container collects discarded paper.')],[M('She put the paper in the trash can, a container meant to keep rubbish on the floor.','She put the paper in the trash can, a container for collecting rubbish.','A trash can holds waste until it can be emptied.')],[Q('trash can.q1','trash can.s1','meaning','What is a trash can used for?','Holding rubbish until it is emptied.','Carrying passengers along street rails.','Storing a student’s grade transcript.','It is a container for rubbish.'),Q('trash can.q2','trash can.s1','context','Where did she put the folded paper?','In the rubbish container beside the desk.','On the trapeze above the stage.','Inside the car’s transmission.','The phrase names a waste container.'),Q('trash can.q3','trash can.s1','distinction','Which object is a trash can?','A bin beside a desk for discarded paper.','A lorry transporting boxes.','A flush-fitting stage door.','The bin collects rubbish.'),Q('trash can.q4','trash can.s1','word-choice','Which sentence is natural?','Please empty the trash can when it is full.','Please transcribe the trash can into the report.','Please transpose the trash can into a lower key.','Containers can be emptied when full.')]);
P('trauma','From Greek trauma, “wound,” through Latin and modern medical usage.',[C('trauma.s1','心理创伤','The accident left her with trauma that made driving difficult for months.','那場事故造成的心理創傷讓她好幾個月都難以開車。','trauma from / after + event','Noun: a very shocking experience with a lasting effect on the mind.','The accident has a continuing psychological effect.'),C('trauma.s2','身体损伤','The surgeon treated the patient’s head trauma after the fall.','病人跌倒後，外科醫生治療了他的頭部外傷。','head / physical trauma','Noun: a serious physical injury.','The patient has bodily damage to the head.')],[M('The doctor called a minor paper cut severe trauma even though there was no serious physical injury or lasting psychological effect.','The doctor called the serious head injury trauma after the fall.','Trauma in this sense is a serious physical injury, not any tiny harmless mark.')],[Q('trauma.q1','trauma.s1','meaning','What does psychological trauma refer to?','A shocking experience with a lasting effect on the mind.','A small object used to catch an animal.','A change in the order of columns.','The first sense concerns lasting psychological effects.'),Q('trauma.q2','trauma.s2','context','What did the surgeon treat after the fall?','A serious physical injury to the head.','A film preview.','A temporary change of school.','Head trauma is a physical injury.'),Q('trauma.q3','trauma.s1','distinction','Which example is psychological trauma?','An accident leaves someone with lasting fear of driving.','A cut that needs one plaster but no lasting effect.','A broken wheel on a tram.','The first has a lasting effect on mental well-being.'),Q('trauma.q4','trauma.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses trauma for bodily injury?','the patient suffered head trauma','the patient remembered a traumatic event','the patient described a lasting psychological trauma','Head trauma names physical injury.')]);
P('travel','From Middle English travailen, “to toil or journey with difficulty,” related to Old French travailler.',[C('travel.s1','出行','They travel by train to the coast every summer.','他們每年夏天都搭火車去海岸旅行。','travel to / from + place; travel by + transport','Verb: go from one place to another.','They move between home and the coast.'),C('travel.s2','旅行活动','Air travel became more affordable after the new route opened.','新航線開通後，航空旅行變得更實惠。','air / business / international travel','Noun: the activity of travelling.','The phrase refers to travelling as an activity.')],[M('They travelled to the coast by staying at home and never going anywhere.','They travelled to the coast by train during the summer holiday.','Travel means go from one place to another, not remain at home.')],[Q('travel.q1','travel.s1','meaning','What do they do when they travel to the coast?','Go from home to another place.','Remain at home throughout the holiday.','Write down the train’s announcements.','The verb sense means go from one place to another.'),Q('travel.q2','travel.s2','context','What became more affordable when air travel costs fell?','The activity of travelling by air.','A particular traveller’s shoes.','A vehicle’s power transmission.','Air travel names the activity or mode of travel.'),Q('travel.q3','travel.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses travel as a verb?','She travels to the clinic twice a week.','International travel can be expensive.','Air travel connects the islands.','The first describes a person going to a place.'),Q('travel.q4','travel.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses travel as a noun?','business travel across the region','travel to the region by bus','they travelled across the region','The phrase names the activity.')]);
P('travel document','A compound phrase describing an official document required or used for international travel.',[C('travel document.s1','国际出行','The border officer checked that each passenger’s travel document was valid.','邊境官員檢查每位乘客的旅行證件是否有效。','a valid travel document','Noun: an official paper, such as a passport, shown when travelling between countries.','The document proves identity or permission for cross-border travel.')],[M('The officer accepted a restaurant menu as a travel document for crossing the border.','The officer checked the passenger’s passport as a travel document for crossing the border.','A travel document is an official paper such as a passport, not an unrelated menu.')],[Q('travel document.q1','travel document.s1','meaning','What might count as a travel document at a border?','An official paper such as a passport.','A restaurant menu.','A film trailer ticket.','The term refers to official travel papers.'),Q('travel document.q2','travel document.s1','context','Why did the officer check that the document was valid?','To confirm it could be used for cross-border travel.','To see whether it listed university grades.','To identify a railway carriage.','A valid passport or similar paper is needed for international travel.'),Q('travel document.q3','travel document.s1','distinction','Which item is a travel document?','A passport presented at immigration.','A bus timetable kept at home.','A transcript of an interview.','A passport is an official travel document.'),Q('travel document.q4','travel document.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','show a valid travel document at the border','transmit a travel document over a tram rail','transplant a travel document into a patient','Border officials inspect travel documents.')]);
P('traveler','North American spelling of traveller, from travel + -er.',[C('traveler.s1','旅途人物','The traveler missed the final train and booked a room near the station.','這名旅客錯過末班火車後，在車站附近訂了房間。','a traveler on / to + journey','Noun: a person travelling, especially away from home.','The person is away on a journey.')],[M('The traveler never left home and made no journey, yet was described as a traveler on the road.','The traveler crossed the region by train and stayed away from home.','A traveler is a person who is on a journey, especially away from home.')],[Q('traveler.q1','traveler.s1','meaning','Who is the traveler in the example?','A person away from home on a journey.','A vehicle that carries goods.','A person who only writes travel documents.','A traveler is someone making a journey.'),Q('traveler.q2','traveler.s1','context','Why did the traveler book a room by the station?','The missed train left them away from home overnight.','The station was the traveler’s permanent home.','They were preparing a blood transfusion.','The traveler is away from home on a journey.'),Q('traveler.q3','traveler.s1','distinction','Which spelling is common in North America?','traveler','traveller only','travelor','Traveler is the North American spelling with one l.'),Q('traveler.q4','traveler.s1','word-choice','Which sentence uses traveler naturally?','The traveler carried a passport and a small bag.','The traveler was the railway’s cargo container.','The traveler was the train’s engine transmission.','A person on a journey may carry travel papers and luggage.')]);
P('traveling','From travel + -ing; it functions as a participle or adjective for going from place to place or designed for journeys.',[C('traveling.s1','旅途用品','She packed her traveling bag with only the items she needed for a week away.','她把一週旅行所需的物品裝進旅行包。','traveling + bag / exhibition / show','Adjective: going from place to place, or designed for use on a journey.','The bag is intended for use while travelling.')],[M('She packed a traveling bag designed to stay permanently fixed in the office and never go on a journey.','She packed a traveling bag designed to carry her belongings on a journey.','A traveling bag is designed for use while travelling.')],[Q('traveling.q1','traveling.s1','meaning','What is a traveling bag designed for?','Carrying belongings on a journey.','Staying permanently attached to an office desk.','Transporting blood into a patient.','The adjective describes something designed for a journey.'),Q('traveling.q2','traveling.s1','context','Why did she pack a traveling bag?','She needed a bag for a week away from home.','She was transcribing an interview.','She was changing a song’s key.','The bag is used while travelling.'),Q('traveling.q3','traveling.s1','distinction','Which phrase uses traveling as an adjective?','a traveling exhibition that visits several towns','they are traveling to the coast','traveling is expensive in winter','The exhibition goes from place to place.'),Q('traveling.q4','traveling.s1','word-choice','Which item is a traveling bag?','A case made for carrying clothes on a trip.','A fixed cabinet that cannot be moved.','A container used only for rubbish.','The case is designed for journey use.')]);
P('traveller','British spelling of traveler, from travel + -er; the source also records a religious pilgrim sense.',[C('traveller.s1','旅途人物','The traveller asked the station clerk which train went north.','旅客詢問車站職員哪班火車往北開。','a traveller on a journey','Noun: a person travelling to a place far away.' ,'The person is away on a journey.'),C('traveller.s2','朝圣者','Medieval travellers walked the old road to the shrine as an act of devotion.','中世紀的朝聖者懷著虔誠之心沿著古道步行前往聖地。','a traveller to a sacred place','Noun: a person journeying to a sacred place for religious reasons.','The destination is a shrine visited for faith.')],[M('The medieval traveller made a religious pilgrimage to the shrine but was described as someone with no sacred destination.','The medieval traveller walked to the shrine on a religious pilgrimage.','In the specific source sense, a traveller can be a pilgrim going to a sacred place.')],[Q('traveller.q1','traveller.s1','meaning','What does a traveller do in the general sense?','Journeys to a place away from home.','Operates a radio transmitter.','Transposes music into another key.','The general noun is a person making a journey.'),Q('traveller.q2','traveller.s2','context','Why were the medieval travellers walking to the shrine?','They were making a religious pilgrimage.','They were delivering a trainload of grain.','They were attending a school transfer.','The source includes a religious traveller going to a sacred place.'),Q('traveller.q3','traveller.s1','distinction','Which phrase uses the general journey sense?','a traveller missed the northbound train','a traveller walked to a shrine as an act of devotion','a pilgrim reached the sacred site','The missed train sentence only says a person was journeying.'),Q('traveller.q4','traveller.s2','word-choice','Which person is a traveller in the religious sense?','A pilgrim walking to a sacred shrine.','A commuter riding a tram to work.','A student requesting a grade transcript.','A pilgrimage to a sacred destination matches the special sense.')]);
P('traverse','From Old French traverser, from Latin transversare, “to cross over.”',[C('traverse.s1','穿越地形','The survey team traversed the ridge before the afternoon storm arrived.','測量隊在午後暴風雨來臨前穿越了山脊。','traverse + terrain or region','Verb: cross a place or area from one side to the other.','The team crosses the ridge.'),C('traverse.s2','艰难行程','Their traverse of the plateau took six days and required careful planning.','他們穿越高原的行程花了六天，必須仔細規劃。','a traverse of + difficult area','Noun: an act of crossing a place, especially a long or difficult one.','The noun names the crossing itself.')],[M('The team traversed the ridge by remaining at the starting point and never crossing it.','The team traversed the ridge from the western slope to the eastern slope.','To traverse an area is to cross it from one side to another.')],[Q('traverse.q1','traverse.s1','meaning','What did the survey team do when it traversed the ridge?','Crossed it from one side to the other.','Stayed at the starting point.','Recorded the ridge as a transcript.','The verb means cross an area.'),Q('traverse.q2','traverse.s2','context','What took six days in the example?','The team’s difficult crossing of the plateau.','The team’s blood transfusion.','The time needed to publish a film trailer.','The noun traverse names the act of crossing.'),Q('traverse.q3','traverse.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses traverse as a verb?','The hikers traversed the desert from west to east.','The traverse of the pass took two days.','A difficult traverse requires supplies.','The hikers perform the crossing action.'),Q('traverse.q4','traverse.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses traverse as a noun?','a week-long traverse across the glacier','they traverse the glacier carefully','the glacier was traversed yesterday','The noun phrase names the crossing itself.')]);
P('travesty','From Italian travestire “to disguise,” through French travesti; the figurative noun is a grotesque distortion.',[C('travesty.s1','荒谬歪曲','The report called the rushed hearing a travesty of justice because no witnesses were heard.','報告稱這場倉促的聽證會是對正義的嘲弄，因為沒有聽取任何證人的證詞。','a travesty of + serious ideal or thing','Noun: a false and ridiculous representation of something serious.','The hearing fails so badly that it distorts justice.'),C('travesty.s2','讽刺模仿','The sketch travesties the official ceremony by copying its gestures in an absurd way.','這段短劇用荒唐的方式模仿官方儀式的動作，形成滑稽的歪曲。','travesty + a person, work, or ceremony (verb)','Verb: imitate or present something grotesquely or misleadingly.','The sketch imitates the ceremony in a distorted way.')],[M('The fair hearing was a travesty of justice because every witness was heard and the evidence was carefully weighed.','The rushed hearing was a travesty of justice because no witness was heard and the evidence was ignored.','A travesty of justice is a grotesque distortion of justice, not a fair process.')],[Q('travesty.q1','travesty.s1','meaning','Why was the hearing called a travesty of justice?','It distorted justice by excluding witnesses and evidence.','It followed a fair process and heard everyone.','It was a successful journey across a plateau.','The noun describes a ridiculous or false representation of something serious.'),Q('travesty.q2','travesty.s2','context','How did the sketch travesty the ceremony?','It imitated the ceremony in an absurd, distorted way.','It documented the event word for word.','It carried the ceremony’s equipment by train.','The verb means imitate or present in a grotesque way.'),Q('travesty.q3','travesty.s1','distinction','Which phrase uses travesty as a noun?','a travesty of justice','the actor travesties the minister','the sketch travesties the ceremony','The first names a distorted representation.'),Q('travesty.q4','travesty.s2','word-choice','Which sentence uses travesty as a verb?','The parody travesties the solemn speech.','The parody was a travesty of the speech.','The speech was transcribed exactly.','“Travesties” is the action of grotesquely imitating the speech.')]);
P('tray','Recorded in Middle English; the word’s deeper origin is uncertain.',[C('tray.s1','餐饮与收纳','She carried four cups across the room on a tray with raised edges.','她用一個有凸起邊緣的托盤把四個杯子端過房間。','carry / serve something on a tray','Noun: a flat board with raised edges for carrying food, drinks, or papers.','The raised rim helps keep the cups from sliding off.')],[M('She balanced the cups on a tray with no surface, leaving them floating unsupported.','She balanced the cups on a flat tray with raised edges.','A tray is a flat carrying board, often with raised edges.')],[Q('tray.q1','tray.s1','meaning','What is a tray used for?','Carrying food, drinks, or papers on a flat board.','Catching an animal in the woods.','Broadcasting a radio signal.','A tray is a flat carrying surface, often with a raised rim.'),Q('tray.q2','tray.s1','context','Why did the tray have raised edges?','To help keep the cups from sliding off.','To let the cups be pulled behind a car.','To change the cups into another form.','Raised edges help hold items while carrying.'),Q('tray.q3','tray.s1','distinction','Which item is a tray?','A flat board with a rim used to carry drinks.','A suspended bar for acrobats.','A hidden panel that lifts from the stage.','The board is a carrying tray.'),Q('tray.q4','tray.s1','word-choice','Which phrase is natural?','serve tea on a tray','transmit tea on a tray','transplant tea into a tray','Tea and cups can be carried or served on a tray.')]);
const supplement=(w,context,q)=>{const p=globalThis.RA.depthPatches[w];p.contexts.push(context);p.quiz[3]=q;};
supplement('trail',C('trail.s3','动作与位置','Her scarf trailed behind her as she hurried down the station steps.','她匆忙走下車站階梯時，圍巾拖在身後。','trail behind / on the ground','Verb: follow someone, or hang or drag behind.','The scarf hangs and drags behind her as she moves.'),Q('trail.q4','trail.s3','grammar','Which sentence uses trail to mean hang or drag behind?','Her long scarf trailed on the pavement.','We followed a trail through the woods.','The team trailed by two goals.','The scarf hangs and drags behind its wearer.'));
supplement('train',C('train.s2','事件序列','One delayed shipment set off a train of problems for the entire factory.','一批貨物延誤，引發了整座工廠接連不斷的問題。','a train of + events, thoughts, or people','Noun: a series of connected events, thoughts, or moving people or animals.','The shipment delay leads to a sequence of problems.'),Q('train.q4','train.s2','context','What does “a train of problems” mean here?','A connected series of problems caused by the delay.','A set of railway carriages carrying the factory goods.','A group of workers learning new skills.','A train can figuratively mean a connected sequence of events.'));
supplement('trample',C('trample.s3','声音','We heard the trample of horses on the road before the riders appeared.','騎手現身前，我們先聽見馬匹在路上沉重踏步的聲音。','the trample of + feet / hooves','Noun: the act or sound of people or animals stepping heavily.','The repeated heavy hoofbeats are audible on the road.'),Q('trample.q4','trample.s3','context','What did the trample of horses announce?','The heavy repeated sound of their hooves on the road.','A legal violation of the riders’ rights.','A small device set to catch an animal.','The noun can name the sound or act of heavy stepping.'));
supplement('transcendent',C('transcendent.s2','哲学术语','In the philosopher’s notes, “a transcendent” names something understood as going beyond ordinary experience.','在哲學家的筆記中，名詞用法的「超越者」指被理解為超越日常經驗的事物。','a transcendent (rare noun use)','Noun, rare: something that transcends the ordinary.','The word is substantivized to name what lies beyond the ordinary.'),Q('transcendent.q4','transcendent.s2','distinction','In the rare noun use, what does “a transcendent” refer to?','Something that goes beyond ordinary experience.','A routine event with no unusual quality.','A person who carries freight across a continent.','The source records a rare noun for something transcending the ordinary.'));
})();
